{"drafts":[{"assumptions":["Where assumptions conflict, the later or human answer wins: Q-6 (cancel only from Received/Confirmed) over ASM-11; Q-8 (inactive company users cannot sign in) over ASM-19; Q-7 (shared templates, answered by Hamza) over ASM-1 (templates out of scope); ASM-33 (only Out of stock blocks) over ASM-4; ASM-39 (no tax) over ASM-6; ASM-40 (basket kept across sign-ins) over ASM-14.","Q-5 ('addresses managed by staff/admin') overrides ASM-2 for delivery addresses only; all other customer company fields are maintained by Administrators only (ASM-2).","ASM-45 is read as: Office Staff is the standard staff role and Administrator has every Office Staff permission plus administration; customer users have the Buyer role.","Order emails go to the Buyer who placed the order; for staff-created orders they go to the customer company's contact email.","Vehicle search uses the compatibility fields admins enter (make, model, year, engine, variant); fuel type is not captured because ASM-49 does not include it.","Payment term, booking horizon, low-stock threshold, cutoff, timezone, non-working days, holiday dates, link validities and number prefixes are system-wide settings with defaults 30 days / 30 days / admin-set / 14:00 / admin-set / Sat+Sun / none / 1 h reset, 7 days invitation / ORD-, INV-.","Retired products are hidden from catalogue browsing and search but kept on historical orders and invoices.","A single currency is used for all prices."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"p95 server response time ≤ 1,000 ms","text":"Catalogue search, category filter and vehicle search response time with 50,000 active products and 100 concurrent users."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"p95 ≤ 2,000 ms","text":"Checkout submission response time under 100 concurrent users."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"Completes in ≤ 10 minutes; a failed run leaves 0 product rows changed","text":"Nightly stock import duration for a 100,000-row CSV."},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"≥ 99% within 5 minutes","text":"Transactional emails (confirmation, amendment, rejection, out-for-delivery, reset, invitation) handed to the email service after the triggering event."},{"id":"NFR-5","metric":"0 plaintext passwords in storage; minimum length 12 characters","text":"Passwords stored only as salted hashes with a slow hash (bcrypt cost ≥ 12 or Argon2id); minimum password length."},{"id":"NFR-6","metric":"TLS 1.2 or higher on 100% of endpoints; HTTP requests redirected to HTTPS","text":"All traffic encrypted in transit."},{"id":"NFR-7","metric":"Sessions expire after 30 minutes of inactivity","text":"Idle session expiry."},{"id":"NFR-8","metric":"All main flows pass on the latest 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari and Firefox","text":"Browser support (ASM-27)."},{"id":"NFR-9","metric":"0 WCAG 2.1 AA failures in an audit of these flows","text":"Accessibility of main flows: sign-in, catalogue, basket, checkout, order history, invoices (ASM-28)."},{"id":"NFR-10","metric":"≥ 99.5% monthly uptime excluding announced maintenance","text":"Service availability, hosted in one cloud region of the client's account (ASM-29)."},{"id":"NFR-11","metric":"Max 10 MB per file","text":"Product images and invoice PDFs stored in cloud storage (ASM-25)."}],"outOfScope":["Exposing the Customer Account Manager role in this release; only the role model is kept extensible (Q-1)","Customers creating or editing their own delivery addresses (Q-5)","Backorders and ordering quantities above imported stock (request §8, ASM-33)","Online card payments or any payment provider integration; ASM-23 (Stripe) contradicts request §32 'The portal does not take online card payments in this phase'","Tax calculation and tax lines on orders/invoices (ASM-39)","Volume, promotional, discount and effective-dated pricing; one price per product per price list (request §10)","Writing stock or orders back to the ERP; the portal only reads the CSV (request §9)","Route planning for deliveries (request §22)","SMS or push notifications; email only from fixed templates (ASM-42)","Migrating existing customers, products, price lists or compatibility data; system starts empty with set-up seed data (ASM-15)","Nested categories (ASM-48)","Full-text search engine and relevance ranking (ASM-50)","Custom report builder (ASM-51)","Languages other than English (ASM-53)","Bulk import of vehicle compatibility data; entered manually (ASM-49)","Separate 'Rejected' order status (ASM-41)"],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active Buyer user of an active customer company with known password","id":"AC-1.1","level":"api","then":"The response is success, a session token/cookie is issued, and a subsequent call to the user's profile endpoint returns that user","when":"POST sign-in with the correct email and password"},{"given":"An existing user and an email address that belongs to no user","id":"AC-1.2","level":"api","then":"Both responses are rejected with the same status code and the same message 'Invalid email or password', and no session is issued","when":"POST sign-in once with a wrong password for the existing user and once with the unknown email"}],"ears":"When a user submits an email address and password that match an active user of an active customer company or an active staff account, the portal shall start an authenticated session for that user.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active user with 4 consecutive failed sign-in attempts","id":"AC-2.1","level":"api","then":"Both attempts are rejected with the message that the account is temporarily locked and no session is issued","when":"A 5th attempt with a wrong password is made, followed by an attempt with the correct password 1 minute later"},{"given":"A user account locked at time T","id":"AC-2.2","level":"api","then":"Sign-in succeeds and the failed-attempt counter is reset to 0","when":"The user signs in with the correct password at T+15 minutes and 1 second"},{"given":"A user with 4 consecutive failed attempts","id":"AC-2.3","level":"api","then":"The account is not locked (counter restarted after the success)","when":"The user signs in successfully and then fails once"}],"ears":"If a user account records 5 consecutive failed sign-in attempts, then the portal shall lock that account for 15 minutes and reject every sign-in attempt for it during the lock with a 'temporarily locked' message.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-20"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An existing user and reset validity of 1 hour","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"One email is sent to the outbound email service addressed to the user containing a reset link, and the API response is identical to the response for an unknown email","when":"POST forgot-password with the user's email"},{"given":"A reset link issued at time T with 1 hour validity","id":"AC-3.2","level":"api","then":"The reset is rejected as expired and the password is unchanged","when":"The link is used at T+61 minutes"}],"ears":"When a user requests a password reset for an email address of an existing user, the portal shall email that address a single-use reset link that expires after the configured reset validity (default 1 hour).","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-46"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A locked account and a valid reset link for it","id":"AC-4.1","level":"api","then":"The reset succeeds with a confirmation, sign-in with the new password succeeds, and sign-in with the old password fails","when":"The user sets a new password through the link and then signs in with the new password"},{"given":"A reset link already used once","id":"AC-4.2","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected and the password is unchanged","when":"The same link is submitted again"}],"ears":"When a user submits a new password through a valid unused reset link, the portal shall replace the password, clear any active sign-in lock on the account, and invalidate the link.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-47"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Administrator session and an active customer company","id":"AC-5.1","level":"api","then":"A pending user is created linked to the company, and one invitation email with a link is sent to the outbound email service","when":"POST invite for a Buyer of that company"},{"given":"A pending invitation","id":"AC-5.2","level":"api","then":"A new invitation email is sent and the earlier link is rejected when used","when":"The Administrator resends the invitation"},{"given":"An invitation sent at time T with 7 day validity","id":"AC-5.3","level":"api","then":"The link is rejected as expired and the user stays pending","when":"The link is used at T+7 days and 1 minute"}],"ears":"When an Administrator invites a user with name, email, role and (for a Buyer) customer company, the portal shall create a pending invitation and email an invitation link that expires after the configured invitation validity (default 7 days).","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","ASM-46"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A pending invited user with a valid link","id":"AC-6.1","level":"api","then":"The account status is Active and sign-in succeeds","when":"The user submits a password through the link and then signs in"}],"ears":"When an invited user sets a password through a valid unexpired invitation link, the portal shall make the user's account active.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Buyer with an open session whose company has 2 orders and 1 invoice","id":"AC-7.1","level":"api","then":"Both calls are rejected, and Office Staff can still retrieve the 2 orders and 1 invoice","when":"An Administrator sets the company inactive and the Buyer then calls the order list and tries to sign in again"},{"given":"An inactive company","id":"AC-7.2","level":"api","then":"Its active users can sign in again","when":"An Administrator reactivates it"},{"given":"A deactivated user","id":"AC-7.3","level":"api","then":"Sign-in is rejected and the user's previously placed orders remain listed for the company","when":"The user signs in with the correct password"}],"ears":"If a user is deactivated or belongs to a customer company set to inactive, then the portal shall reject that user's sign-in and any further requests from that user's existing sessions while keeping all orders and invoices linked to the user or company.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","Q-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in user","id":"AC-8.1","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected as unauthenticated","when":"The user signs out and then reuses the old session token on the order list endpoint"}],"ears":"When a signed-in user signs out, the portal shall invalidate that user's session.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Buyer A of company X and an order and invoice of company Y","id":"AC-9.1","level":"api","then":"Every request returns not found/forbidden and no company Y data is in the response","when":"Buyer A requests the order detail, invoice detail and invoice PDF of company Y by id"},{"given":"Two Buyers B1 and B2 of company X, with an order placed by B2","id":"AC-9.2","level":"api","then":"The list includes B2's order and its invoice","when":"B1 lists orders and invoices"}],"ears":"The portal shall return orders, invoices, prices, delivery addresses and account information to a Buyer only when they belong to that Buyer's own customer company.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-5","Q-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Administrator session","id":"AC-10.1","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected as an invalid role","when":"The Administrator invites a user with role 'Account Manager'"},{"given":"A Buyer session","id":"AC-10.2","level":"api","then":"Each call is rejected with forbidden","when":"The Buyer calls the staff order queue, a customer edit and a product edit endpoint"},{"given":"An Administrator session and a Received order","id":"AC-10.3","level":"api","then":"The order becomes Confirmed","when":"The Administrator confirms the order"}],"ears":"The portal shall allow only the roles Buyer, Office Staff and Administrator to be assigned to users, where Administrator holds every Office Staff permission in addition to administration permissions.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","Q-1","ASM-45"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Administrator session and an active price list","id":"AC-11.1","level":"api","then":"The company is stored and returned with the same values","when":"The Administrator creates a company with all listed fields"},{"given":"An Office Staff session","id":"AC-11.2","level":"api","then":"The call is rejected with forbidden, while the company detail endpoint returns the company","when":"Staff call the company edit endpoint"}],"ears":"Where the user is an Administrator, the portal shall allow creating, editing and setting active/inactive customer companies with company name, account number, primary contact, contact email, contact phone, billing address and assigned price list.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","ASM-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Companies 'Smith Motors' (ACC-100) and 'Fleetline' (ACC-200)","id":"AC-12.1","level":"api","then":"The first search returns only Smith Motors and the second only Fleetline","when":"Staff search 'smith' and then '200'"}],"ears":"When Office Staff search customer companies with text, the portal shall return companies whose name or account number contains the text, ignoring case.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Office Staff session and a company","id":"AC-13.1","level":"api","then":"The address is listed for the company and offered to its Buyers at checkout","when":"Staff add a delivery address"},{"given":"A Buyer session","id":"AC-13.2","level":"api","then":"The call is rejected with forbidden, while listing the company's addresses succeeds","when":"The Buyer calls the create or edit delivery address endpoint"}],"ears":"Where the user is Office Staff or an Administrator, the portal shall allow adding, editing and removing a customer company's delivery addresses (label, address lines 1-2, city, state/region, postal code, country, contact person, contact phone).","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","Q-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active product 'Brake Pad Set' code BP-1234 brand 'Brembo' MPN P85020, and a retired product 'Brake Disc'","id":"AC-14.1","level":"api","then":"Each search returns 'Brake Pad Set' and none returns the retired product","when":"The Buyer searches 'brake', 'bp-12', 'p8502' and 'brem'"}],"ears":"When a Buyer searches the catalogue with text, the portal shall return active products whose product name, distributor product code, manufacturer part number or manufacturer/brand contains the text, ignoring case.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10","ASM-50"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"3 active products in 'Filters' and 2 in 'Brake system'","id":"AC-15.1","level":"api","then":"The results contain 3, 2 and 5 products respectively","when":"The Buyer lists with category 'Filters', then 'Brake system', then no category"}],"ears":"When a Buyer selects a category filter, the portal shall return only active products assigned to that category, and shall return all active products when the filter is cleared.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10","ASM-48"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P1 compatible with Ford Focus 2018 1.0 EcoBoost and product P2 compatible with Ford Fiesta 2018","id":"AC-16.1","level":"api","then":"Only P1 is returned; searching make Ford alone returns P1 and P2","when":"The Buyer searches make Ford, model Focus, year 2018"}],"ears":"When a Buyer searches by vehicle using make and optionally model, year, engine and variant, the portal shall return active products that have a compatibility entry matching every supplied value.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10","ASM-49"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active product with all fields set and a price on the Buyer's price list","id":"AC-17.1","level":"api","then":"The item contains all listed fields with the price from the Buyer's price list","when":"The Buyer lists the catalogue"}],"ears":"The portal shall return each catalogue list item with product image, product name, distributor product code, manufacturer, unit of sale, pack size, the Buyer's price and stock status.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Out of stock product compatible with 2 vehicles","id":"AC-18.1","level":"api","then":"The product is returned with status 'Out of stock' and both vehicles listed","when":"The Buyer requests the product detail"}],"ears":"When a Buyer opens a product, the portal shall return its image, name, product code, manufacturer part number, manufacturer, description, unit of sale, pack size, the Buyer's price, stock status and list of compatible vehicles.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P priced 10.00 on 'Standard' and 8.50 on 'Fleet', company X on 'Fleet' and company Y on 'Standard'","id":"AC-19.1","level":"api","then":"The X Buyer sees 8.50 and the Y Buyer sees 10.00, and neither response contains the other price","when":"A Buyer of X and a Buyer of Y view P"}],"ears":"When a Buyer views prices, the portal shall show for each product the price from the price list assigned to the Buyer's customer company.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-11"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active product P with no price on the Buyer's price list","id":"AC-20.1","level":"api","then":"P is shown with 'price on request' and no price, and the add is rejected with a message","when":"The Buyer views P and then adds P to the basket"}],"ears":"If an active product has no price on the Buyer's assigned price list, then the portal shall show it as 'price on request' and reject adding it to a basket.","id":"REQ-20","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-11","ASM-31"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Administrator session and price list 'Dealer' with product P at 20.00","id":"AC-21.1","level":"api","then":"'Dealer' holds exactly one price for P, 18.00","when":"The Administrator sets P to 18.00 on 'Dealer'"},{"given":"Company X on 'Standard'","id":"AC-21.2","level":"api","then":"Buyers of X then see 'Dealer' prices","when":"The Administrator assigns 'Dealer' to X"}],"ears":"Where the user is an Administrator, the portal shall allow creating and renaming price lists, setting, editing and removing one price per product on a price list, and assigning or changing the price list of a customer company.","id":"REQ-21","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Price list 'Fleet' assigned to active company X","id":"AC-22.1","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected listing company X and 'Fleet' stays active","when":"The Administrator deactivates 'Fleet'"},{"given":"Price list 'Old' assigned to no active company","id":"AC-22.2","level":"api","then":"'Old' becomes inactive and can no longer be assigned","when":"The Administrator deactivates 'Old'"}],"ears":"If an Administrator deactivates a price list that is assigned to any active customer company, then the portal shall reject the deactivation and name the assigned companies.","id":"REQ-22","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-17","ASM-44"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An order with 2 lines of 3 x 10.00 and 1 x 5.00","id":"AC-23.1","level":"api","then":"The order total and invoice total are both 35.00 and no tax line is present","when":"The order is delivered and its invoice is retrieved"}],"ears":"The portal shall show all product prices, basket totals, order totals and invoice totals excluding tax, without calculating tax.","id":"REQ-23","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-16","ASM-39"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Low-stock threshold 5","id":"AC-24.1","level":"unit","then":"It returns Out of stock, Low stock, Low stock and In stock","when":"The stock status calculator's public method is called with quantities 0, 1, 5 and 6"}],"ears":"The portal shall derive a product's stock status as Out of stock when quantity is 0 or less, Low stock when quantity is from 1 up to the configured low-stock threshold, and In stock when quantity is above the threshold.","id":"REQ-24","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-12","ASM-36"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Products A (qty 10) and B (qty 0), threshold 5, and a valid CSV with A=3 and B=50 in the configured folder","id":"AC-25.1","level":"job","then":"A has qty 3 and status Low stock, B has qty 50 and status In stock, and an import log row with status Success and 2 rows imported exists","when":"The stock import job runs"}],"ears":"When the scheduled stock import runs and finds a valid ERP CSV (product code, quantity) in the configured location, the portal shall update the quantity and stock status of each listed known product and record the import as successful with its run time and row counts.","id":"REQ-25","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","I-3","ASM-34"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product A with qty 10 and a CSV whose second row has quantity 'abc'","id":"AC-26.1","level":"job","then":"A still has qty 10, no product changed, and an import log row with status Failed and the reason is recorded","when":"The stock import job runs"},{"given":"No file in the configured location","id":"AC-26.2","level":"job","then":"Stock data is unchanged and a Failed import log row is recorded","when":"The stock import job runs"}],"ears":"If the ERP CSV is missing, unreadable, has wrong columns or contains a non-numeric quantity, then the portal shall keep all previous stock data unchanged and record the import as failed with the reason.","id":"REQ-26","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Products A (qty 10) and C (qty 7), and a valid CSV with A=4 and unknown code ZZZ=9","id":"AC-27.1","level":"job","then":"A has qty 4, C still has qty 7, and the import log lists ZZZ as skipped","when":"The stock import job runs"}],"ears":"When the ERP CSV is otherwise valid, the portal shall skip and log rows with unknown product codes and keep the previous stock of products not present in the file.","id":"REQ-27","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","ASM-35"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"One successful and one failed import run","id":"AC-28.1","level":"api","then":"Both runs are returned with their status and the failed one shows its reason; a Buyer request is forbidden","when":"Staff request the import history"}],"ears":"When Office Staff or Administrators request the stock import history, the portal shall return each import run with time, status, rows imported, skipped codes and failure reason.","id":"REQ-28","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Buyer whose price for P is 12.50 and for Q is 4.00","id":"AC-29.1","level":"api","then":"The basket holds P line total 25.00, Q line total 4.00, subtotal 29.00","when":"The Buyer adds 2 x P and 3 x Q, changes Q to 1, signs out and signs in again"},{"given":"A basket with line P","id":"AC-29.2","level":"api","then":"The basket no longer contains P and the subtotal excludes it","when":"The Buyer removes P"}],"ears":"The portal shall keep one saved basket per user that supports adding a product with a quantity, changing a quantity, removing a line, and returns the line price, line total and subtotal, persisting it across sign-ins until checkout or clearing.","id":"REQ-29","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-40"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P with status Out of stock","id":"AC-30.1","level":"api","then":"The add is rejected with an out-of-stock message","when":"The Buyer adds P to the basket"},{"given":"A basket line Q that became Out of stock after it was added","id":"AC-30.2","level":"api","then":"Submission is rejected naming Q and no order is created; after removing Q submission succeeds","when":"The Buyer submits checkout"},{"given":"Product L with status Low stock and quantity 2","id":"AC-30.3","level":"api","then":"The order is accepted (quantity is not checked against stock)","when":"The Buyer adds 10 x L and checks out"}],"ears":"If a basket line's product has stock status Out of stock or is retired, then the portal shall reject adding it and block checkout until that line is removed.","id":"REQ-30","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-13","ASM-33"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Cutoff 14:00, Saturday and Sunday non-working, no holidays","id":"AC-31.1","level":"unit","then":"It returns Tuesday, Wednesday and the following Tuesday","when":"The delivery date calculator's public method is called for Monday 13:59, Monday 14:00 and Friday 15:00"},{"given":"Tuesday configured as a holiday date","id":"AC-31.2","level":"unit","then":"It returns Wednesday","when":"The calculator is called for Monday 13:00"},{"given":"Business timezone Europe/London","id":"AC-31.3","level":"unit","then":"It treats the order as after cutoff and returns Wednesday","when":"The calculator is called for an instant that is 13:30 UTC during British Summer Time (14:30 local) on a Monday"}],"ears":"The portal shall compute the earliest delivery date as the next working day for orders placed before the configured cutoff (default 14:00) and the second working day for orders placed at or after the cutoff, in the configured business timezone, where working days exclude configured non-working weekdays and holiday dates.","id":"REQ-31","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-37"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An order placed Monday 15:00 with weekends non-working","id":"AC-32.1","level":"api","then":"All three submissions are rejected; submitting Wednesday succeeds","when":"The Buyer submits with delivery date Tuesday, then Saturday, then a working day 31 days ahead"}],"ears":"If a submitted delivery date is not a working day between the earliest delivery date and the configured booking horizon (default 30 days from the order date), then the portal shall reject the order submission with the list of allowed dates.","id":"REQ-32","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-38"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"P added to the basket at 10.00 and then repriced to 11.00 on the Buyer's list","id":"AC-33.1","level":"api","then":"Submission is rejected with P listed old 10.00 new 11.00, the basket line is 11.00, and a second submission with confirmation creates the order at 11.00","when":"The Buyer submits checkout"}],"ears":"If the checkout price check finds a basket line whose price differs from the Buyer's current price list, then the portal shall update the line to the current price, return the old and new prices, and reject submission until the Buyer confirms again.","id":"REQ-33","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","I-11","ASM-32"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Prefix 'ORD-' and last order number ORD-000122","id":"AC-34.1","level":"api","then":"Order ORD-000123 is returned with status Received, a timeline entry (Received, time, Buyer), the lines and prices, and the basket is empty","when":"The Buyer submits a valid checkout"},{"given":"Order ORD-000123 with P at 11.00","id":"AC-34.2","level":"api","then":"ORD-000123 still shows P at 11.00 and the same total","when":"An Administrator changes P to 13.00 on the price list"},{"given":"Address belonging to another company","id":"AC-34.3","level":"api","then":"Submission is rejected","when":"The Buyer submits checkout with it"},{"given":"A newly created order","id":"AC-34.4","level":"api","then":"The order appears with status Received","when":"Office Staff list the order queue"}],"ears":"When a Buyer submits a valid checkout with a delivery address of their company, a delivery date and an optional note, the portal shall create an order with the next sequential order number using the configured prefix, the lines with order-time prices, the address, date and note, status Received with a timeline entry, and empty the basket.","id":"REQ-34","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-13","I-4","ASM-43"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An order in Confirmed","id":"AC-35.1","level":"api","then":"The first two are rejected and Picking succeeds with a timeline entry naming the staff user and time","when":"Staff request Out for delivery, then Received, then Picking"},{"given":"An order in Picking","id":"AC-35.2","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected","when":"Staff request Cancelled"}],"ears":"When a status change is requested on an order, the portal shall allow only the next forward step (Received→Confirmed→Picking→Out for delivery→Delivered) or Cancelled from Received or Confirmed, recording status, date/time and acting user or system in the order timeline.","id":"REQ-35","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","Q-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order whose line quantity staff changed from 5 to 3","id":"AC-36.1","level":"api","then":"Status is Confirmed, confirmer and time are recorded, and one email to the recipient containing the order number and the change 5→3 is sent to the outbound email service","when":"Staff confirm it"},{"given":"A Received order with a line that is now Out of stock","id":"AC-36.2","level":"api","then":"Confirmation is rejected naming the line and the status stays Received","when":"Staff confirm it"}],"ears":"When Office Staff confirm a Received order whose lines are all not Out of stock or retired and whose customer company is active, the portal shall set it to Confirmed, record the confirming user and time, and email the order's recipient a confirmation with order number, lines, quantities, prices, total, delivery address and date, and any staff quantity changes.","id":"REQ-36","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","I-4","ASM-42"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order with line P quantity 5","id":"AC-37.1","level":"api","then":"The order shows P quantity 3 with the recalculated total and an amendment entry (P, 5→3, user, time) visible in order detail","when":"Staff set P to 3"},{"given":"A Confirmed order","id":"AC-37.2","level":"api","then":"The edit is rejected","when":"Staff try to change a quantity"}],"ears":"While an order is Received, the portal shall allow Office Staff to change line quantities, remove lines, change the delivery date under the delivery date rules, change the delivery address to another address of the same company, and edit the note, recording each amendment with user, time, old and new values.","id":"REQ-37","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","I-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order with line P quantity 5 and line Q","id":"AC-38.1","level":"api","then":"An email to the recipient listing P 5→3 and Q removed is sent to the outbound email service","when":"Staff change P to 3 and remove Q"}],"ears":"When Office Staff change a line quantity or remove a line on an order, the portal shall email the order's recipient the order number and each changed line with old and new quantity.","id":"REQ-38","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","ASM-42"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order","id":"AC-39.1","level":"api","then":"Status is Cancelled, the timeline shows staff-rejected with the reason, user and time, and an email with the reason is sent","when":"Staff reject it with reason 'Account on hold'"},{"given":"A Received order","id":"AC-39.2","level":"api","then":"The rejection is rejected as invalid and the status stays Received","when":"Staff reject it with an empty reason"}],"ears":"When Office Staff reject a Received or Confirmed order with a reason, the portal shall set it to Cancelled marked staff-rejected, record the reason, user and time, and email the order's recipient the order number and reason.","id":"REQ-39","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","ASM-41","Q-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company X on price list 'Fleet' with P at 8.50","id":"AC-40.1","level":"api","then":"The order has line total 17.00, status Received, created-by-staff with the staff user, and appears in X Buyers' order history","when":"Staff create an order for X with 2 x P"},{"given":"Staff creating an order Monday 15:00","id":"AC-40.2","level":"api","then":"The order is rejected per the cutoff rule","when":"Staff choose Tuesday delivery"}],"ears":"When Office Staff submit an order on behalf of a customer company with a delivery address, product lines, delivery date and optional note, the portal shall create the order at that company's price-list prices under the same delivery date rules, marked as created by staff with the staff user.","id":"REQ-40","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","I-14","ASM-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An order in Picking","id":"AC-41.1","level":"api","then":"One email with the order number and out-for-delivery text is sent to the recipient via the outbound email service","when":"Staff set it to Out for delivery"}],"ears":"When an order changes to Out for delivery, the portal shall email the order's recipient a message identifying the order number and stating it is out for delivery.","id":"REQ-41","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","I-5","ASM-42"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Orders of companies X and Y in statuses Received and Picking","id":"AC-42.1","level":"api","then":"Only X's Received orders are returned with all listed fields","when":"Staff filter by customer X and status Received"}],"ears":"When Office Staff list the order queue, the portal shall return orders with order number, customer, order date, requested delivery date, total and status, filterable by customer, order date range and status.","id":"REQ-42","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"For date D: one Confirmed, one Picking, one Received and one Delivered order","id":"AC-43.1","level":"api","then":"The CSV has a header row with the listed columns and exactly 2 data rows (the Confirmed and Picking orders)","when":"Staff export the delivery list for D"}],"ears":"When Office Staff export the delivery list for a date (default today), the portal shall return a CSV of orders with that delivery date in Confirmed, Picking or Out for delivery status containing order number, customer, delivery address, contact name and phone, delivery date, line summary, note and status.","id":"REQ-43","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","ASM-52"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company X with 3 orders (one Cancelled) placed by two Buyers and staff","id":"AC-44.1","level":"api","then":"Only the Cancelled order is returned; unfiltered returns all 3","when":"A Buyer of X lists orders filtered by status Cancelled"}],"ears":"When a Buyer lists orders, the portal shall return all orders of the Buyer's company, including staff-created ones, with order number, order date, delivery date, delivery address, total and status, filterable by order date range and status.","id":"REQ-44","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-15","Q-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Confirmed order with one staff amendment","id":"AC-45.1","level":"api","then":"All listed fields are returned including timeline entries Received and Confirmed and the amendment","when":"A Buyer of the company opens it"}],"ears":"When a Buyer or Office Staff open an order, the portal shall return order number, order date, customer, delivery address, requested delivery date, current status, status timeline, lines with quantity, unit price and line total, order total, note and staff amendments.","id":"REQ-45","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Received order","id":"AC-46.1","level":"api","then":"Status becomes Cancelled with a timeline entry naming the Buyer","when":"A Buyer of the company cancels it"},{"given":"A Confirmed order","id":"AC-46.2","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected with a contact-the-office message and status stays Confirmed","when":"A Buyer cancels it"}],"ears":"If a Buyer requests cancellation of an order that is not in Received status, then the portal shall reject it with a message to contact the distributor office.","id":"REQ-46","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A past order with P (now 9.00, was 8.00), retired R and Out of stock S","id":"AC-47.1","level":"api","then":"The basket contains P at 9.00 with the past quantity, R and S are returned as unavailable, and the number of orders is unchanged","when":"The Buyer repeats the order"}],"ears":"When a Buyer repeats a previous order, the portal shall add each line whose product is active, priced on the Buyer's current price list and not Out of stock to the Buyer's basket at the current price, and return the other lines flagged as unavailable, without creating an order.","id":"REQ-47","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Buyer B1 of company X saves template 'Weekly Workshop Order' with P x 4","id":"AC-48.1","level":"api","then":"B2 sees the template and B2's basket contains P x 4 at the current price","when":"Buyer B2 of X lists templates and adds it to the basket"},{"given":"The same template","id":"AC-48.2","level":"api","then":"The template is not returned","when":"A Buyer of company Y lists templates"}],"ears":"Where a Buyer saves the basket as a named template, the portal shall make the template visible to all users of the same customer company for viewing, adding its items to the basket at current prices with unavailable items flagged, and deletion.","id":"REQ-48","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","I-15","Q-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Prefix 'INV-', last invoice INV-000050, and an order Out for delivery","id":"AC-49.1","level":"api","then":"Invoice INV-000051 exists for the order with all listed fields and status Unpaid","when":"Staff set it to Delivered"},{"given":"An order in Picking","id":"AC-49.2","level":"api","then":"No invoice or placeholder for that order is returned","when":"The Buyer lists invoices"}],"ears":"When an order changes to Delivered, the portal shall create an invoice with the next sequential invoice number using the configured prefix, customer, billing address, order number, invoice date, lines with quantity and price, total, and payment status Unpaid.","id":"REQ-49","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","I-5","ASM-43","ASM-30"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Payment term 30 days and an unpaid invoice dated 1 March","id":"AC-50.1","level":"unit","then":"It returns Unpaid on 31 March and Overdue on 1 April","when":"The invoice status method is evaluated on 31 March and on 1 April"},{"given":"A paid invoice dated 1 January","id":"AC-50.2","level":"unit","then":"It returns Paid","when":"Status is evaluated on 1 April"}],"ears":"The portal shall report an unpaid invoice as Overdue when the current date in the business timezone is later than the invoice date plus the configured payment term in days.","id":"REQ-50","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Invoice INV-000051 of company X","id":"AC-51.1","level":"api","then":"The response has content type application/pdf and its text contains the invoice number, order number, every line and the total","when":"A Buyer of X downloads its PDF"},{"given":"Company X with 2 invoices","id":"AC-51.2","level":"api","then":"Both are returned with number, date, total and payment status","when":"A Buyer of X lists invoices"}],"ears":"When a Buyer or Office Staff request an invoice PDF, the portal shall return a PDF containing invoice number, customer, billing address, order number, invoice date, lines, quantities, prices, total and payment status.","id":"REQ-51","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","I-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Overdue invoice","id":"AC-52.1","level":"api","then":"The invoice shows Paid, payment date 2026-11-02 and the staff user; a Buyer calling the same endpoint is forbidden","when":"Staff mark it paid with payment date 2026-11-02"}],"ears":"When Office Staff mark an invoice as paid with a payment date, the portal shall set its status to Paid and record the payment date and the recording user.","id":"REQ-52","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P on a past order","id":"AC-53.1","level":"api","then":"P is absent from catalogue search and still appears on the past order detail","when":"The Administrator retires P"},{"given":"An Office Staff session","id":"AC-53.2","level":"api","then":"The call is rejected with forbidden","when":"Staff call the product edit endpoint"}],"ears":"Where the user is an Administrator, the portal shall allow adding, editing and retiring products with name, manufacturer part number, distributor product code, description, category, manufacturer/brand, unit of sale and pack size, while retired products remain shown on historical orders and invoices.","id":"REQ-53","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","I-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P with image img1","id":"AC-54.1","level":"api","then":"Both uploads are rejected and P still shows img1","when":"The Administrator uploads an 11 MB image and then a .exe file"},{"given":"Product P with image img1","id":"AC-54.2","level":"api","then":"P's catalogue item returns img2","when":"The Administrator uploads a 2 MB image img2"}],"ears":"If an Administrator uploads a product image that is not an image file or is larger than 10 MB, then the portal shall reject the upload and keep the product's current image.","id":"REQ-54","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","ASM-25"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P with no compatibility","id":"AC-55.1","level":"api","then":"P's detail lists exactly the remaining entry and vehicle search for it returns P","when":"The Administrator adds 2 vehicle entries and removes 1"}],"ears":"Where the user is an Administrator, the portal shall allow adding and removing vehicle compatibility entries (make, model, model year, engine, variant) on a product, with any number of entries per product.","id":"REQ-55","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","I-17","ASM-49"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Category 'Exhaust'","id":"AC-56.1","level":"api","then":"'Exhaust' no longer appears in the customer category list","when":"The Administrator retires it"}],"ears":"Where the user is an Administrator, the portal shall allow creating, editing and retiring single-level categories and assigning products to them, hiding retired categories from customer filters.","id":"REQ-56","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","I-17","ASM-48"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active Office Staff user U","id":"AC-57.1","level":"api","then":"U's status is Inactive then Active and U can sign in after reactivation","when":"The Administrator deactivates U and then reactivates U"},{"given":"A Buyer of company X","id":"AC-57.2","level":"api","then":"The Buyer then sees Y's orders and not X's","when":"The Administrator moves the Buyer to company Y"}],"ears":"Where the user is an Administrator, the portal shall allow listing users with role, company and account status, deactivating and reactivating users, changing a user's role, and associating a Buyer with a customer company.","id":"REQ-57","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Cutoff 14:00","id":"AC-58.1","level":"api","then":"The returned earliest date is Wednesday","when":"The Administrator sets the cutoff to 12:00 and a Buyer requests the earliest delivery date at Monday 13:00"},{"given":"An Office Staff session","id":"AC-58.2","level":"api","then":"The call is rejected with forbidden","when":"Staff call the settings update endpoint"}],"ears":"Where the user is an Administrator, the portal shall allow setting the order cutoff time, business timezone, non-working weekdays, holiday dates, booking horizon, low-stock threshold, invoice payment term, reset-link and invitation validity, and order and invoice number prefixes.","id":"REQ-58","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","ASM-37","ASM-36","Q-3","ASM-38","ASM-46","ASM-43"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P named 'Oil Filter'","id":"AC-59.1","level":"api","then":"An audit entry exists with user A, time, product P, action Edit, field name 'Oil Filter'→'Oil Filter OF-1'","when":"Administrator A renames it to 'Oil Filter OF-1'"},{"given":"Price list 'Fleet' with P at 8.50","id":"AC-59.2","level":"api","then":"An audit entry records the price change 8.50→9.00 with user and time","when":"An Administrator sets P to 9.00"}],"ears":"When a product, category, price list or price, customer company or user is created, edited or retired/deactivated, the portal shall record an audit entry with the acting user, time, entity, action and each changed field's old and new value.","id":"REQ-59","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","Q-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Existing audit entries","id":"AC-60.1","level":"api","then":"Both are rejected with forbidden, while an Administrator receives the entries filterable by entity type and date range","when":"An Office Staff user and a Buyer request the audit history"}],"ears":"If a user who is not an Administrator requests the audit history, then the portal shall reject the request with forbidden.","id":"REQ-60","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","Q-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"In range: company X orders of 30.00 and 20.00 and a Cancelled X order of 100.00; product P sold 5 units for 50.00","id":"AC-61.1","level":"api","then":"X shows 2 orders, value 50.00; P shows 5 units, 50.00; the CSV contains the same rows; a Buyer request is forbidden","when":"Staff request the reports and the CSV export for that range"}],"ears":"When Office Staff or Administrators request the sales or product report for a date range, the portal shall return order count and order value per customer and quantity and value sold per product for non-cancelled orders, with a CSV export of the same rows.","id":"REQ-61","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7","ASM-51"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"2 Received, 1 Picking, 1 order due today, 3 Unpaid and 1 Overdue invoice, and 1 failed import after the last success","id":"AC-62.1","level":"api","then":"The counts are Received 2, Picking 1, due today 1, outstanding invoices 4, failed imports 1","when":"Staff request the dashboard"}],"ears":"When Office Staff open the dashboard, the portal shall return counts of Received orders, Confirmed orders, Picking orders, Out for delivery orders, orders with today's delivery date, Unpaid or Overdue invoices, and failed stock imports since the last successful import.","id":"REQ-62","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-7"]}],"suggestions":["Add fuel type to vehicle compatibility data so the vehicle search in request §7.4 can filter by it.","Confirm whether the exact delivery-list CSV columns and the invoice PDF layout must match an existing client template.","Consider a per-customer payment term instead of a single global one if customers have different credit terms.","Consider an alert email to admins when the nightly stock import fails, in addition to the dashboard count.","Consider letting staff cancel Picking orders with a reason if operations need it; currently blocked by Q-6.","Consider customer-specific delivery cutoffs or delivery zones in a later phase."]},{"assumptions":["Where assumptions from two rounds conflict, the later round (ASM-30 onward) and the human answers (Q-1..Q-8) win: basket kept across sign-ins (ASM-40, not ASM-14); no tax calculated (ASM-39, not ASM-6); quantity not checked against stock (ASM-33, not ASM-4).","Q-8 overrides ASM-19: users of an inactive company cannot sign in at all.","Q-6 overrides ASM-11: staff can cancel or reject only from Received or Confirmed.","Q-7 (templates shared across the company) is taken to mean saved basket templates are in scope, which overrides ASM-1.","ASM-45 ('administrator and standard user') is read as: Administrators can also do all Office Staff operations. The three user-facing roles are still Buyer, Office Staff and Administrator, as the request and Q-1 describe.","ASM-23 (Stripe card payments) contradicts the request, which says the portal takes no online card payments in this phase, so it is not applied.","Order emails go to the user who placed the order; for orders staff create, they go to the company's contact email.","Passwords must be at least 10 characters. The request sets no policy, so this is our choice.","A stock file is invalid as a whole if any row has a non-integer or negative quantity, if a required column is missing, or if it has no data rows. Valid files have columns product code and quantity, matched on distributor product code.","Low stock means a quantity above 0 and at or below the threshold.","Product images may be JPEG, PNG or WebP, up to 10 MB (ASM-25).","Order notes are limited to 1000 characters.","Sales and product reports count non-cancelled orders by order date.","The system starts empty, with seed data that includes at least one Administrator account for set-up (ASM-15).","Prices use a single currency."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"0 serious or critical violations from an automated axe scan of each listed page, plus a passing manual keyboard-only walkthrough of all 7 flows","text":"Main customer flows (sign-in, catalogue, product detail, basket, checkout, order history, invoices) meet WCAG 2.1 AA."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"100% of main-flow manual test cases pass on each of the 8 browser versions","text":"The portal works on the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari and Firefox."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"p95 response ≤ 1.0 s with 50,000 active products and 50 concurrent users","text":"Catalogue search and filtering respond within a set time."},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"p95 response ≤ 500 ms at 50 concurrent users","text":"Basket, checkout and order API operations respond within a set time."},{"id":"NFR-5","metric":"≤ 10 minutes for a 50,000-row file","text":"The nightly stock import completes within a set time."},{"id":"NFR-6","metric":"≥ 99% handed to the provider within 5 minutes of the triggering event","text":"Order and account emails reach the email provider soon after the trigger."},{"id":"NFR-7","metric":"Argon2id or bcrypt with cost ≥ 12; 0 plaintext or reversible password values in storage or logs","text":"Passwords are stored only as salted adaptive hashes."},{"id":"NFR-8","metric":"TLS 1.2 or higher on 100% of endpoints; plain HTTP requests are redirected or refused","text":"All traffic is encrypted."},{"id":"NFR-9","metric":"Tokens contain ≥ 128 bits of randomness","text":"Reset and invitation links can't be guessed."},{"id":"NFR-10","metric":"≥ 99.5% monthly uptime, excluding announced maintenance","text":"The portal is available to customers and staff."},{"id":"NFR-11","metric":"0 portal operations that delete or edit these records","text":"Audit entries, order timelines, amendments and payment records cannot be deleted through the portal."},{"id":"NFR-12","metric":"p95 ≤ 3 s per PDF","text":"Invoice PDFs are generated within a set time."},{"id":"NFR-13","metric":"100% of UI and email text in English; all data stored in 1 configured region","text":"The portal is English-only and hosted in one cloud region in the client's account."}],"outOfScope":["Customer Account Manager role exposed to users (Q-1); the role model only needs to allow adding it later","Customers creating or editing their own delivery addresses (Q-5)","Backorders and ordering quantities beyond stock (request §8)","Checking ordered quantity against imported stock quantity (ASM-33)","Online card payments and payment-provider integration (request §32 says no online card payments in this phase; ASM-23 not applied)","Payment method and partial payment recording (request §32 leaves payment method open; only payment date and user are recorded)","Tax calculation on prices, orders or invoices (ASM-39)","Volume, promotional, discount and effective-dated pricing (request §10)","Nested categories (ASM-48)","Full-text search engine and relevance ranking (ASM-50)","Custom report builder (ASM-51)","Importing compatibility data from external sources (ASM-49)","Migrating existing customers, products, price lists or compatibility data (ASM-15)","SMS or push notifications (ASM-42)","Route planning (request §22)","Writing stock or orders back to the ERP (request §9)","Languages other than English and more than one currency (ASM-53)","Reproducing an existing client invoice template (request §31 open point; a standard layout is used)"],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active Buyer buyer@a.test with password 'Correct#Pass1' belonging to active company A","id":"AC-1.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 200, a session token is issued and the returned role is Buyer","when":"POST sign-in with buyer@a.test / 'Correct#Pass1'"},{"given":"An active Office Staff user staff@dist.test","id":"AC-1.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 200 and the returned role is Office Staff","when":"POST sign-in with correct credentials"}],"ears":"When a user submits an email and password that match an active user whose customer company (if any) is active, the portal shall create an authenticated session and return the user's role.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active user buyer@a.test","id":"AC-2.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 401 with message 'Invalid email or password' and no session token","when":"POST sign-in with buyer@a.test and a wrong password"},{"given":"No user with email nobody@x.test exists","id":"AC-2.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 401 with the same status, message and body shape as AC-2.1","when":"POST sign-in with nobody@x.test and any password"}],"ears":"If a sign-in attempt uses an unknown email or a wrong password, then the portal shall reject it with the identical message 'Invalid email or password' and create no session.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active user with 5 consecutive wrong-password attempts ending at time T","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 423 (or 401) with a 'temporarily locked' message and no session token","when":"POST sign-in with the correct password at T+1 minute"},{"given":"An account locked at time T","id":"AC-3.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 200 and a session is issued","when":"POST sign-in with the correct password at T+15 minutes 1 second"},{"given":"An active user","id":"AC-3.3","level":"api","then":"Both correct attempts return 200 (a successful sign-in resets the failure count)","when":"4 wrong attempts, then 1 correct attempt, then 4 wrong attempts, then 1 correct attempt are made"}],"ears":"If an account reaches 5 consecutive failed sign-in attempts, then the portal shall lock the account for 15 minutes and reject every sign-in attempt during the lock, including ones with the correct password, with a message that the account is temporarily locked.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-20"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active user buyer@a.test","id":"AC-4.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 200 with message 'If an account exists, a reset email has been sent' and one email containing a reset link is sent to buyer@a.test via the email provider","when":"POST password-reset request for buyer@a.test"},{"given":"No user with nobody@x.test","id":"AC-4.2","level":"api","then":"Response is identical to AC-4.1 and no email is sent","when":"POST password-reset request for nobody@x.test"},{"given":"A user whose account is currently locked","id":"AC-4.3","level":"api","then":"A reset email is sent to the user","when":"POST password-reset request for that user's email"}],"ears":"When a user requests a password reset for an email address, the portal shall email a single-use reset link valid for the configured reset period (default 1 hour) to that address if it belongs to a user, and shall return the same confirmation message whether or not the address belongs to a user.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-46","ASM-47"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A valid reset link for buyer@a.test","id":"AC-5.1","level":"api","then":"Sign-in with 'NewPassw0rd!' returns 200 and sign-in with the old password returns 401","when":"The user submits new password 'NewPassw0rd!'"},{"given":"A reset link that has already been used once","id":"AC-5.2","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected as invalid and the password is unchanged","when":"The link is submitted again with another password"},{"given":"A reset link issued at time T with the default 1-hour period","id":"AC-5.3","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected as expired and the password is unchanged","when":"It is submitted at T+61 minutes"},{"given":"An account locked 2 minutes ago and a valid reset link","id":"AC-5.4","level":"api","then":"Sign-in returns 200 within the original 15-minute lock window","when":"The user completes the reset and signs in with the new password"},{"given":"A valid reset link","id":"AC-5.5","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected with a message stating the 10-character minimum and the link stays usable","when":"The user submits a 9-character password"}],"ears":"When a user submits a new password of at least 10 characters through an unused, unexpired reset link, the portal shall replace the password, invalidate the link and clear any sign-in lock on the account.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-46","ASM-47"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in Buyer with session token S","id":"AC-6.1","level":"api","then":"The GET returns 401","when":"The Buyer signs out and then calls GET orders with token S"}],"ears":"When a signed-in user signs out, the portal shall invalidate that user's session token.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"No session token","id":"AC-7.1","level":"api","then":"Each returns 401 with no product, order or invoice data","when":"GET catalogue products, GET orders and GET invoices are called"}],"ears":"If a request without a valid session targets any portal operation other than sign-in, password reset and invitation acceptance, then the portal shall reject it with 401 and return no data.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in Buyer","id":"AC-8.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 403","when":"GET staff order queue"},{"given":"A signed-in Office Staff user","id":"AC-8.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 403","when":"POST create product"},{"given":"A signed-in Administrator","id":"AC-8.3","level":"api","then":"Response is 200","when":"GET staff order queue"}],"ears":"If a signed-in user calls an operation outside their role's permissions (Buyer: customer ordering operations; Office Staff: staff operations; Administrator: administration operations plus all Office Staff operations), then the portal shall reject the call with 403.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","ASM-45"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Buyer of company A and order ORD-000050 of company B","id":"AC-9.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 404 with no order data","when":"The Buyer calls GET order ORD-000050"},{"given":"Buyer of company A and invoice INV-000010 of company B","id":"AC-9.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 404 and no PDF is returned","when":"The Buyer requests the PDF of INV-000010"},{"given":"Buyer of company A and a delivery address of company B","id":"AC-9.3","level":"api","then":"Response is 404","when":"The Buyer calls GET on that address id"}],"ears":"If a Buyer requests an order, invoice, invoice PDF, price list, delivery address or company account record belonging to another customer company, then the portal shall respond with 404 and return none of that record's data.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-3","I-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A with Buyers U1 and U2; U1 placed ORD-000001 and staff created ORD-000002 for company A","id":"AC-10.1","level":"api","then":"Both ORD-000001 and ORD-000002 are listed","when":"U2 calls GET orders"},{"given":"Invoice INV-000001 for ORD-000001 placed by U1","id":"AC-10.2","level":"api","then":"INV-000001 is listed","when":"U2 calls GET invoices"}],"ears":"The portal shall show a Buyer every order and invoice of the Buyer's customer company, including orders placed by other users of that company and orders created by staff on its behalf.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","Q-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in Administrator","id":"AC-11.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 400 and no invitation is created","when":"POST invitation with role 'Account Manager'"},{"given":"A signed-in Administrator","id":"AC-11.2","level":"api","then":"Exactly Buyer, Office Staff and Administrator are returned","when":"GET the list of assignable roles"}],"ears":"The portal shall accept only the roles Buyer, Office Staff and Administrator when an administrator invites a user or changes a user's role.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in Administrator and active company A","id":"AC-12.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 201, the user is listed with status Pending and one invitation email is sent to new.buyer@a.test","when":"POST invitation for new.buyer@a.test as Buyer of company A"},{"given":"A signed-in Administrator","id":"AC-12.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 400","when":"POST invitation with role Buyer and no customer company"},{"given":"An existing user with email buyer@a.test","id":"AC-12.3","level":"api","then":"Response is 409 and no email is sent","when":"POST invitation for buyer@a.test"}],"ears":"When an administrator invites a user with name, email, role and (for a Buyer) customer company, the portal shall create a pending invitation valid for the configured invitation period (default 7 days) and email an acceptance link to that address.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","ASM-46"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A pending invitation issued 1 day ago","id":"AC-13.1","level":"api","then":"The user status becomes Active and sign-in with that password returns 200","when":"The user sets password 'Welcome2Portal'"},{"given":"An invitation issued at time T with default 7-day period","id":"AC-13.2","level":"api","then":"The request is rejected as expired and the user stays Pending","when":"It is used at T+7 days 1 minute"}],"ears":"When an invited user sets a password of at least 10 characters through an unexpired invitation link, the portal shall activate the account.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-46"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A pending invitation with link L1","id":"AC-14.1","level":"api","then":"Using L1 is rejected as invalid and using L2 activates the account","when":"The Administrator resends it, producing link L2"}],"ears":"When an administrator resends a pending invitation, the portal shall email a new acceptance link with a fresh validity period and invalidate the earlier link.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","ASM-46"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active Buyer U1 with an open session who placed ORD-000001","id":"AC-15.1","level":"api","then":"U1's next request on the open session returns 401, U1's sign-in is rejected with an 'account deactivated' message, and ORD-000001 is still listed for staff and other Buyers of the company","when":"An Administrator deactivates U1"}],"ears":"When an administrator deactivates a user, the portal shall reject that user's sign-in attempts and requests on their existing sessions while keeping every order and invoice linked to the user.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","I-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A deactivated Buyer U1","id":"AC-16.1","level":"api","then":"U1's status is Active and U1's sign-in returns 200","when":"An Administrator reactivates U1"},{"given":"Office Staff user S1","id":"AC-16.2","level":"api","then":"S1 can call POST create product and receive 201","when":"An Administrator changes S1's role to Administrator"},{"given":"Users in each of the four statuses","id":"AC-16.3","level":"api","then":"Each user is returned with role, company and the correct status","when":"An Administrator calls GET users"}],"ears":"The portal shall let an administrator list users with role, customer company and account status (Pending, Active, Locked, Deactivated), change a user's role, change a Buyer's customer company and reactivate a deactivated user.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A set to inactive with active Buyer U1","id":"AC-17.1","level":"api","then":"Sign-in is rejected with a message that the account is inactive","when":"U1 signs in with correct credentials"},{"given":"Company A inactive with existing orders","id":"AC-17.2","level":"api","then":"The company's orders are returned","when":"Office Staff call GET orders filtered by company A"},{"given":"Company A reactivated","id":"AC-17.3","level":"api","then":"Sign-in returns 200 and U1's earlier orders are listed","when":"U1 signs in and calls GET orders"}],"ears":"While a customer company is inactive, the portal shall reject sign-in for every user of that company and keep the company's orders and invoices.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","Q-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in Administrator and active price list 'Standard'","id":"AC-18.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 201 and GET returns all submitted fields","when":"POST company with all fields, account number C-1001 and one delivery address"},{"given":"Existing company with account number C-1001","id":"AC-18.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 409","when":"POST another company with account number C-1001"},{"given":"A signed-in Administrator","id":"AC-18.3","level":"api","then":"Response is 400","when":"POST company with no delivery address"},{"given":"A signed-in Office Staff user","id":"AC-18.4","level":"api","then":"Response is 403 and the company is unchanged","when":"PUT edit on company C-1001"}],"ears":"The portal shall let administrators create and edit customer companies with company name, unique account number, primary contact, contact email, contact phone, billing address, at least one delivery address, an assigned active price list and active/inactive status.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","ASM-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Companies 'Smith Motors' (C-1001) and 'Jones Fleet' (C-2002)","id":"AC-19.1","level":"api","then":"The first search returns only Smith Motors and the second only Jones Fleet, each with details, users, addresses and price list","when":"Office Staff search 'smith' and then 'C-20'"}],"ears":"When an Office Staff user searches customers by a partial company name or account number, the portal shall return the matching companies with their details, users, delivery addresses and assigned price list.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-4","ASM-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A with 2 delivery addresses","id":"AC-20.1","level":"api","then":"Both addresses are returned with label, lines, city, region, postal code, country, contact person and phone","when":"A Buyer of company A calls GET addresses"},{"given":"A Buyer of company A","id":"AC-20.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 403","when":"The Buyer calls POST or PUT on an address"}],"ears":"The portal shall show a Buyer the delivery addresses of the Buyer's company as read-only.","id":"REQ-20","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","Q-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active product 'Brake Pad Set' code BP-1023, part number MPN-77A, brand Bosch","id":"AC-21.1","level":"api","then":"Each search returns 'Brake Pad Set'","when":"The Buyer searches 'brak', 'bp-10', 'mpn-77' and 'bosch' in turn"},{"given":"Retired product 'Brake Hose' and active product 'Air Filter'","id":"AC-21.2","level":"api","then":"No products are returned","when":"The Buyer searches 'brake hose'"}],"ears":"When a Buyer searches the catalogue with a text term, the portal shall return active products whose product name, distributor product code, manufacturer part number or manufacturer/brand contains the term, ignoring case.","id":"REQ-21","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10","ASM-50"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"3 active products in 'Filters' and 2 in 'Brake system'","id":"AC-22.1","level":"api","then":"The results are 3 products, then 2 products, then all 5 products","when":"The Buyer filters by 'Filters', then by 'Brake system', then clears the filter"}],"ears":"When a Buyer filters the catalogue by one category, the portal shall return only active products assigned to that category, and when the filter is cleared it shall return all active products.","id":"REQ-22","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10","ASM-48"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P1 compatible with Ford/Focus/2018/1.0 EcoBoost/Petrol and P2 compatible with Ford/Fiesta/2018","id":"AC-23.1","level":"api","then":"Only P1 is returned","when":"The Buyer searches make Ford, model Focus, year 2018"},{"given":"The same data","id":"AC-23.2","level":"api","then":"P1 and P2 are returned","when":"The Buyer searches make Ford only"}],"ears":"When a Buyer searches by vehicle using any combination of make, model, year, engine, fuel type and variant, the portal shall return active products that have a compatibility entry matching every supplied value.","id":"REQ-23","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10","ASM-49"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active product with all fields set and price 12.50 on the Buyer's price list, stock In stock","id":"AC-24.1","level":"api","then":"The entry contains image URL, name, code, manufacturer, unit, pack size, price 12.50 and status 'In stock'","when":"The Buyer lists the catalogue"}],"ears":"The portal shall return each catalogue list entry with product image, product name, distributor product code, manufacturer, unit and pack size, the Buyer's price (or 'price on request') and stock status.","id":"REQ-24","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active product with 2 compatibility entries","id":"AC-25.1","level":"api","then":"All listed fields are returned, including both compatibility entries","when":"The Buyer calls GET product detail"},{"given":"Active product with stock status Out of stock","id":"AC-25.2","level":"api","then":"The product is returned with status 'Out of stock'","when":"The Buyer calls GET product detail"}],"ears":"When a Buyer opens an active product, the portal shall return its image, name, distributor product code, manufacturer, description, unit, pack size, the Buyer's price (or 'price on request'), stock status and list of compatible vehicles.","id":"REQ-25","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","I-3","I-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Order ORD-000001 containing product P1, then P1 retired by an Administrator","id":"AC-26.1","level":"api","then":"P1 is absent from the catalogue, GET P1 detail returns 404 for the Buyer, and ORD-000001 still shows P1's name, code and order-time price","when":"The Buyer lists the catalogue and opens ORD-000001"}],"ears":"While a product is retired, the portal shall exclude it from Buyer catalogue listing, search and detail while still showing its stored name, code and price on existing orders and invoices.","id":"REQ-26","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","I-17","I-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P priced 10.00 on 'Standard' and 8.00 on 'Fleet'; company A assigned 'Standard', company B assigned 'Fleet'","id":"AC-27.1","level":"api","then":"Buyer A sees 10.00 and Buyer B sees 8.00","when":"Buyers of A and B each open P"},{"given":"Company A reassigned from 'Standard' to 'Fleet'","id":"AC-27.2","level":"api","then":"Buyer A sees 8.00","when":"Buyer A opens P"}],"ears":"The portal shall price every product shown to a Buyer, or to staff acting for a customer, from the price list assigned to that customer's company.","id":"REQ-27","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-11"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active product Q with no price on company A's price list","id":"AC-28.1","level":"api","then":"Detail shows 'price on request' and the add returns 422 with the basket unchanged","when":"Buyer A opens Q and then POSTs Q to the basket"}],"ears":"If an active product has no price on the customer's assigned price list, then the portal shall show it as 'price on request' and reject adding it to a basket.","id":"REQ-28","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-11","ASM-31","ASM-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A delivered order with lines totalling 100.00","id":"AC-29.1","level":"api","then":"The invoice total is 100.00 and no tax line or tax amount appears","when":"The invoice is retrieved and its PDF generated"}],"ears":"The portal shall present all prices, line totals, order totals and invoice totals as net amounts excluding tax, without calculating or adding any tax.","id":"REQ-29","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-16","ASM-39"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in Administrator","id":"AC-30.1","level":"api","then":"A Buyer of company A sees P at 9.50","when":"The Administrator creates 'Dealer', sets P to 9.00, edits it to 9.50 and assigns 'Dealer' to company A"},{"given":"'Dealer' already has a price for P","id":"AC-30.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 409 and only one price for P exists","when":"The Administrator adds a second price for P to 'Dealer'"},{"given":"P priced on 'Dealer'","id":"AC-30.3","level":"api","then":"Buyers on 'Dealer' see P as 'price on request'","when":"The Administrator removes P from 'Dealer'"}],"ears":"The portal shall let administrators create and rename price lists, set, edit and remove one price per product on a price list, and assign or change the price list of a customer company.","id":"REQ-30","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Price list 'Fleet' assigned to active company B","id":"AC-31.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 409 naming company B and 'Fleet' stays active","when":"An Administrator deactivates 'Fleet'"},{"given":"Price list 'Old' assigned to no active company","id":"AC-31.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 200 and 'Old' cannot be assigned to companies","when":"An Administrator deactivates 'Old'"}],"ears":"If an administrator tries to deactivate a price list assigned to any active customer company, then the portal shall reject the deactivation and list the assigned companies.","id":"REQ-31","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-17","ASM-44"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"ORD-000001 contains 2 x P at 10.00 (total 20.00)","id":"AC-32.1","level":"api","then":"ORD-000001 still shows unit price 10.00 and total 20.00","when":"An Administrator changes P to 12.00 on the same price list"}],"ears":"When a price on a price list changes, the portal shall keep the order-time prices on existing orders and invoices unchanged.","id":"REQ-32","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Low-stock threshold set to 5","id":"AC-33.1","level":"unit","then":"It returns Out of stock, Low stock, Low stock and In stock respectively","when":"The stock-status calculator is called directly with quantities 0, 1, 5 and 6"}],"ears":"The portal shall derive each product's stock status from its imported quantity as Out of stock when the quantity is 0 or less, Low stock when it is above 0 and at or below the configured low-stock threshold, and In stock when it is above the threshold.","id":"REQ-33","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-12","ASM-36"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Products BP-1023 (qty 10) and AF-200 (qty 0), threshold 5, and a valid file with rows BP-1023,3 and AF-200,40","id":"AC-34.1","level":"job","then":"BP-1023 shows Low stock (qty 3), AF-200 shows In stock (qty 40), and an import record with status Success and 2 rows imported exists","when":"The stock import job runs"}],"ears":"When the scheduled stock import reads a valid ERP CSV from the configured location, the portal shall update the quantity and stock status of each listed known product and record a successful import with timestamp and row counts.","id":"REQ-34","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","I-3","ASM-34"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Products BP-1023 (qty 10) and AF-200 (qty 7), and a file with rows BP-1023,4 and XX-999,5","id":"AC-35.1","level":"job","then":"BP-1023 has qty 4, AF-200 keeps qty 7, and the import record lists XX-999 as a skipped unknown code","when":"The stock import job runs"}],"ears":"When a valid stock file contains rows with unknown product codes or omits known products, the portal shall skip and log the unknown rows and keep the previous quantity of each omitted product.","id":"REQ-35","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","ASM-35","ASM-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"BP-1023 with qty 10 and a file whose second row has quantity 'abc'","id":"AC-36.1","level":"job","then":"BP-1023 still has qty 10 and an import record with status Failed and a reason naming the invalid row exists","when":"The stock import job runs"},{"given":"A file missing the quantity column","id":"AC-36.2","level":"job","then":"No product quantity changes and a Failed import record is created","when":"The stock import job runs"}],"ears":"If a stock file is unreadable, has no data rows, lacks the product code or quantity column, or contains any row with a non-integer or negative quantity, then the portal shall change no stock data and record a failed import with the failure reason.","id":"REQ-36","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","I-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"BP-1023 with imported qty 10","id":"AC-37.1","level":"api","then":"BP-1023 still shows qty 10","when":"A Buyer orders 4 x BP-1023 and staff confirm and deliver the order"}],"ears":"The portal shall leave imported stock quantities unchanged when orders are placed, amended, confirmed, cancelled or delivered.","id":"REQ-37","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"P at 12.50 and R at 4.00 on the Buyer's price list","id":"AC-38.1","level":"api","then":"Line totals are 25.00 and 12.00 and the subtotal is 37.00","when":"The Buyer adds 2 x P and 3 x R"},{"given":"A basket with 2 x P","id":"AC-38.2","level":"api","then":"Both updates return 400 and the quantity stays 2","when":"The Buyer sets the quantity to 0, then to 1.5"},{"given":"A basket with lines P and R","id":"AC-38.3","level":"api","then":"Only P remains and the subtotal equals P's line total","when":"The Buyer removes R"}],"ears":"The portal shall let a Buyer add a product to the basket, change a line quantity to a positive whole number, remove a line, and see each line's unit price, line total and the basket subtotal.","id":"REQ-38","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","I-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P with stock status Out of stock and a price on the Buyer's list","id":"AC-39.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 422 with an out-of-stock message and the basket is unchanged","when":"The Buyer POSTs P to the basket"},{"given":"Product L with Low stock and imported qty 2","id":"AC-39.2","level":"api","then":"The add succeeds (quantity is not checked against imported stock)","when":"The Buyer adds 10 x L"}],"ears":"If a product's stock status is Out of stock, then the portal shall reject adding it to a basket.","id":"REQ-39","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-13","ASM-33"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Buyer with 2 x P in the basket","id":"AC-40.1","level":"api","then":"The basket contains 2 x P","when":"The Buyer signs out, signs in again and calls GET basket"},{"given":"Buyer U1 of company A has a basket","id":"AC-40.2","level":"api","then":"U2's basket does not contain U1's lines","when":"Buyer U2 of company A calls GET basket"}],"ears":"The portal shall keep one saved basket per user across sign-ins until it is checked out or cleared.","id":"REQ-40","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-40"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Cutoff 14:00, Saturday and Sunday non-working, no holidays","id":"AC-41.1","level":"unit","then":"It returns Tuesday, Wednesday and Wednesday","when":"The delivery-date calculator is called directly with Monday 13:00, Monday 14:00 and Monday 15:00"},{"given":"The same settings","id":"AC-41.2","level":"unit","then":"It returns the following Monday and the following Tuesday","when":"It is called with Friday 13:00 and Friday 15:00"},{"given":"The same settings plus Tuesday configured as a holiday","id":"AC-41.3","level":"unit","then":"It returns Wednesday","when":"It is called with Monday 13:00"},{"given":"Business timezone Europe/London","id":"AC-41.4","level":"unit","then":"It returns Wednesday","when":"It is called with Monday 13:30 UTC during British Summer Time (14:30 local)"}],"ears":"The portal shall calculate the earliest delivery date as the next working day for orders placed before the configured cutoff time (default 14:00) and as the second working day for orders placed at or after it, using the configured business timezone and excluding configured weekly non-working days and holiday dates.","id":"REQ-41","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-37","ASM-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Monday 13:00 submission; earliest date Tuesday","id":"AC-42.1","level":"api","then":"Each submission returns 422 and no order is created","when":"The Buyer submits with delivery date Monday (today), then Saturday, then 31 days ahead"},{"given":"Monday 13:00 submission","id":"AC-42.2","level":"api","then":"The first date is Tuesday, no non-working days appear, and no date is more than 30 days ahead","when":"The Buyer calls GET available delivery dates"}],"ears":"If a submitted order's delivery date is not a working day between the earliest delivery date and the configured maximum days ahead (default 30), then the portal shall reject the submission.","id":"REQ-42","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-38"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Buyer of company A and an address id belonging to company B","id":"AC-43.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 422 (or 404) and no order is created","when":"The Buyer submits an order with that address"}],"ears":"If a submitted order's delivery address does not belong to the customer's company, then the portal shall reject the submission.","id":"REQ-43","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","Q-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A basket with P and R, and R's stock status changed to Out of stock after it was added","id":"AC-44.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 422 identifying line R and no order is created","when":"The Buyer submits the order"},{"given":"The same basket after the Buyer removes R","id":"AC-44.2","level":"api","then":"The order is created","when":"The Buyer submits the order"}],"ears":"If any basket line's product is Out of stock, retired or without a price on the customer's price list at checkout, then the portal shall block order submission and identify those lines until they are removed.","id":"REQ-44","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","I-3","ASM-33"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"2 x P added at 10.00, then P changed to 11.00 on the Buyer's price list","id":"AC-45.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 409 listing P with old 10.00 and new 11.00, the basket line now shows 11.00, and no order is created","when":"The Buyer submits the order"},{"given":"The situation after AC-45.1","id":"AC-45.2","level":"api","then":"The order is created with P at 11.00","when":"The Buyer confirms and submits again"}],"ears":"If a basket line's price differs from the customer's current price at checkout, then the portal shall update the line to the current price, return the changed lines with old and new prices, and refuse submission until the Buyer confirms the updated basket.","id":"REQ-45","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","I-11","ASM-32"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A basket with 2 lines, a selected address, date and note 'Rear gate'","id":"AC-46.1","level":"api","then":"All listed values are returned and GET orders shows no new order","when":"The Buyer calls the checkout review"}],"ears":"When a Buyer requests the checkout review, the portal shall return all lines with quantities, unit prices and line totals, the order total, the selected delivery address, delivery date and order note without creating an order.","id":"REQ-46","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Last order number ORD-000122 and a valid basket","id":"AC-47.1","level":"api","then":"Order ORD-000123 is created with status Received, the lines and prices from the basket, the chosen address, date and note, and GET basket returns an empty basket","when":"The Buyer submits the order"},{"given":"A valid basket","id":"AC-47.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 400 and no order is created","when":"The Buyer submits with a 1001-character note"},{"given":"Order ORD-000123 just submitted","id":"AC-47.3","level":"api","then":"ORD-000123 is listed with status Received","when":"Office Staff call GET order queue"}],"ears":"When a Buyer submits a valid order, the portal shall create it with the next sequential order number (configured prefix, default 'ORD-', 6 digits), its lines at order-time prices, the delivery address, delivery date, optional note of up to 1000 characters and status Received, and then empty the basket.","id":"REQ-47","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","I-1","I-14","ASM-43"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"ORD-000010 with lines P (2 @ 10.00), R (1, now retired) and S (3, now Out of stock); P now 11.00","id":"AC-48.1","level":"api","then":"The basket contains 2 x P at 11.00, R and S are returned flagged unavailable, and no new order exists","when":"The Buyer repeats ORD-000010"}],"ears":"When a Buyer repeats a previous order, the portal shall add each line whose product is active, not Out of stock and priced on the customer's current price list to the basket at the current price, and return the remaining lines flagged as unavailable, without creating an order.","id":"REQ-48","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-15","I-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Buyer U1 of company A with 2 x P and 5 x R in the basket","id":"AC-49.1","level":"api","then":"U2 sees 'Weekly Workshop Order' with 2 x P and 5 x R","when":"U1 saves it as 'Weekly Workshop Order' and Buyer U2 of company A lists templates"},{"given":"The same template","id":"AC-49.2","level":"api","then":"It is not listed and the request returns 404","when":"A Buyer of company B lists templates or requests it by id"}],"ears":"When a user of a customer company saves the basket as a named template, the portal shall store the template's products and quantities and make it available to every user of that company.","id":"REQ-49","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","I-15","Q-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Template with 2 x P (now 11.00) and 1 x R (now retired)","id":"AC-50.1","level":"api","then":"The basket gains 2 x P at 11.00 and R is returned flagged unavailable","when":"A Buyer adds the template to the basket"}],"ears":"When a user adds a template to the basket, the portal shall add each available template line at the customer's current price and return lines whose product is retired, Out of stock or unpriced flagged as unavailable.","id":"REQ-50","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","I-15","Q-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Template created by U1 in company A","id":"AC-51.1","level":"api","then":"Each call succeeds and after deletion the template is no longer listed for U1 or U2","when":"U2 of company A renames it, sets P to 4 and then deletes it"}],"ears":"The portal shall let any user of the owning company rename a template, change its line quantities, remove its lines and delete it.","id":"REQ-51","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","I-15","Q-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A orders: ORD-1 Received on 1 March, ORD-2 Delivered on 5 March","id":"AC-52.1","level":"api","then":"The first result is only ORD-2 and the second only ORD-1, each with all listed fields","when":"A Buyer lists orders filtered by status Delivered, then by date 1–2 March"}],"ears":"The portal shall list a Buyer's company orders with order number, order date, delivery date, delivery address, total and status, filterable by order date range and status.","id":"REQ-52","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-15","Q-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"ORD-000123 confirmed after staff changed P's quantity from 5 to 3","id":"AC-53.1","level":"api","then":"All listed fields are returned, the timeline shows Received then Confirmed, and the amendment shows P quantity 5 to 3","when":"The Buyer opens ORD-000123"}],"ears":"When a Buyer or staff user opens an order, the portal shall return its number, order date, customer, delivery address, requested delivery date, current status, status timeline, lines with quantities, unit prices and line totals, order total, note, whether staff created it, and any staff amendments.","id":"REQ-53","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-15","I-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"ORD-000123 in Received","id":"AC-54.1","level":"api","then":"Status is Cancelled and the timeline's last entry is Cancelled by that Buyer with a timestamp","when":"A Buyer of the company cancels it"}],"ears":"When a Buyer cancels a company order in Received status, the portal shall set it to Cancelled and add a timeline entry naming the Buyer.","id":"REQ-54","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-15","I-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"ORD-000123 in Confirmed","id":"AC-55.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 409 with a 'contact the distributor office' message and the status stays Confirmed","when":"A Buyer of the company cancels it"}],"ears":"If a Buyer tries to cancel an order that is not in Received status, then the portal shall reject the cancellation with a message to contact the distributor office.","id":"REQ-55","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An order in Received","id":"AC-56.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 409 and the status stays Received","when":"Staff set it to Picking"},{"given":"An order in Picking","id":"AC-56.2","level":"api","then":"Both return 409 and the status stays Picking","when":"Staff set it to Confirmed, then to Cancelled"},{"given":"An order in Picking","id":"AC-56.3","level":"api","then":"Response is 200 and the status is Out for delivery","when":"Staff set it to Out for delivery"},{"given":"An order in Delivered or Cancelled","id":"AC-56.4","level":"api","then":"Response is 409","when":"Staff request any status change"}],"ears":"If a staff user requests an order status change other than one step forward along Received, Confirmed, Picking, Out for delivery, Delivered, or Cancelled from Received or Confirmed, then the portal shall reject the change.","id":"REQ-56","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","Q-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"ORD-000123 submitted by Buyer U1 and confirmed by staff S1","id":"AC-57.1","level":"api","then":"It holds Received by U1 and Confirmed by S1, each with a timestamp, in that order","when":"Staff GET the order timeline"}],"ears":"When an order changes status, the portal shall append a timeline entry with the new status, date/time and the user or 'system' that made the change.","id":"REQ-57","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","I-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"ORD-000123 in Received with 5 x P","id":"AC-58.1","level":"api","then":"The order shows 3 x P with a recalculated total and an amendment entry by S1 with old 5 and new 3","when":"Staff S1 changes P to 3"},{"given":"ORD-000123 in Confirmed","id":"AC-58.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 409 and the order is unchanged","when":"Staff change a quantity"},{"given":"ORD-000123 in Received","id":"AC-58.3","level":"api","then":"Response is 422","when":"Staff set the delivery date to a configured holiday"}],"ears":"While an order is in Received status, the portal shall let staff change line quantities, remove lines, change the delivery date within the delivery date rules, change the delivery address to another address of the company and edit the note, recording each change with user, time, field, old value and new value.","id":"REQ-58","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","I-4","I-8","ASM-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"ORD-000123 placed by Buyer U1 with 5 x P and 1 x R","id":"AC-59.1","level":"api","then":"Email to U1 via the email provider contains ORD-000123, 'P: 5 → 3' and 'R: removed'","when":"Staff change P to 3 and remove R"}],"ears":"When staff change a line quantity or remove a line on an order, the portal shall email the order's recipient the order number and each changed line with old and new quantity.","id":"REQ-59","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","ASM-42"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"ORD-000123 in Received with in-stock lines","id":"AC-60.1","level":"api","then":"Status is Confirmed and the timeline shows Confirmed by S1 with a timestamp","when":"Staff S1 confirms it"},{"given":"ORD-000123 in Received with a line whose product is now Out of stock","id":"AC-60.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 422 identifying the line and the status stays Received","when":"Staff confirm it"}],"ears":"When staff confirm a Received order whose customer company is active and whose lines contain no retired or Out of stock product, the portal shall set it to Confirmed and record the confirming user and date/time.","id":"REQ-60","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","I-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"ORD-000123 placed by U1 where staff changed P from 5 to 3","id":"AC-61.1","level":"api","then":"One email to U1 contains ORD-000123, the lines, total, address, date and 'P: 5 → 3'","when":"Staff confirm it"}],"ears":"When an order becomes Confirmed, the portal shall email the order's recipient the order number, lines with quantities and prices, order total, delivery address, delivery date and any quantity changes made by staff.","id":"REQ-61","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","I-5","ASM-42"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"ORD-000123 in Received","id":"AC-62.1","level":"api","then":"Status is Cancelled, the timeline entry is staff-rejected by S1 with the reason, and an email with ORD-000123 and 'Account on hold' goes to the recipient","when":"Staff S1 rejects it with reason 'Account on hold'"},{"given":"ORD-000123 in Received","id":"AC-62.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 400 and the status stays Received","when":"Staff reject it with an empty reason"}],"ears":"When staff reject an order in Received or Confirmed status with a non-empty reason, the portal shall set it to Cancelled marked as staff-rejected, record the reason, user and date/time, and email the order's recipient the order number and reason.","id":"REQ-62","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","ASM-41","Q-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"ORD-000123 in Picking placed by U1","id":"AC-63.1","level":"api","then":"One email to U1 contains ORD-000123 and states it is out for delivery","when":"Staff set it to Out for delivery"}],"ears":"When an order becomes Out for delivery, the portal shall email the order's recipient the order number and a statement that the order is out for delivery.","id":"REQ-63","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","I-5","ASM-42"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company A on price list 'Standard' with P at 10.00","id":"AC-64.1","level":"api","then":"The order is Received with P at 10.00, marked created by S1, and is listed in GET orders for Buyers of company A","when":"Staff S1 creates an order for company A with 2 x P, a company A address and a valid date"},{"given":"Monday 15:00","id":"AC-64.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 422","when":"Staff create an order for Tuesday delivery"},{"given":"Company A and product Q with no price on its list","id":"AC-64.3","level":"api","then":"Response is 422","when":"Staff add Q to the order"}],"ears":"When staff submit an order on behalf of a customer company, the portal shall apply the same pricing, stock, address and delivery date rules as Buyer checkout, create the order in Received status and record the staff user as its creator.","id":"REQ-64","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","I-14","ASM-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Orders for companies A and B in statuses Received and Confirmed","id":"AC-65.1","level":"api","then":"Only company A's Received orders are returned with all listed fields","when":"Staff filter by company A and status Received"}],"ears":"The portal shall show staff an order queue of all orders with order number, customer, order date, requested delivery date, order total and current status, filterable by customer, order date range and status.","id":"REQ-65","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"For 10 March: ORD-1 Confirmed, ORD-2 Received, ORD-3 Out for delivery; ORD-4 Confirmed for 11 March","id":"AC-66.1","level":"api","then":"The CSV has the listed header and rows for ORD-1 and ORD-3 only","when":"Staff export the delivery list for 10 March"}],"ears":"When staff export the delivery list for a date (default today), the portal shall return a CSV of orders with that delivery date in Confirmed, Picking or Out for delivery status, with columns order number, customer, delivery address, contact person, contact phone, delivery date, order lines summary, note and status.","id":"REQ-66","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","ASM-52"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"2 Received, 1 Picking, 1 Out for delivery order, 3 Unpaid and 1 Overdue invoice, and a latest import that Failed","id":"AC-67.1","level":"api","then":"The counts are 2, 1, 1, 3 and 1 and the latest import shows Failed with its reason and time","when":"Staff call GET dashboard"}],"ears":"The portal shall show staff a dashboard with counts of Received, Picking and Out for delivery orders, orders due for delivery today, unpaid and overdue invoices, and the result and time of the latest stock import including any failure reason.","id":"REQ-67","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"ORD-000123 Out for delivery with total 37.00 and last invoice INV-000040","id":"AC-68.1","level":"api","then":"Invoice INV-000041 exists for ORD-000123 with the listed fields, total 37.00 and status Unpaid","when":"Staff set it to Delivered"},{"given":"ORD-000124 in Out for delivery","id":"AC-68.2","level":"api","then":"No invoice for ORD-000124 is listed","when":"A Buyer of the company lists invoices"}],"ears":"When an order becomes Delivered, the portal shall create exactly one invoice for it with the next sequential invoice number (configured prefix, default 'INV-', 6 digits), customer, billing address, order number, invoice date, lines with quantities and order-time prices, total and status Unpaid.","id":"REQ-68","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","I-5","ASM-43","ASM-30"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Payment term 30 days and an unpaid invoice dated 1 March","id":"AC-69.1","level":"unit","then":"It returns Unpaid and Overdue respectively","when":"The invoice status calculator is called directly for 31 March and for 1 April"},{"given":"The same invoice marked Paid on 20 March","id":"AC-69.2","level":"unit","then":"It returns Paid","when":"The calculator is called for 1 May"}],"ears":"The portal shall report an unpaid invoice as Overdue once the current date in the business timezone is later than the invoice date plus the configured payment term in days, and as Unpaid before then.","id":"REQ-69","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","I-5","Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Invoices for companies A (Unpaid) and B (Paid)","id":"AC-70.1","level":"api","then":"The Buyer sees only A's invoice; staff see only B's invoice","when":"A Buyer of A lists invoices, and staff list invoices filtered by status Paid"}],"ears":"The portal shall list invoices with invoice number, order number, invoice date, total and payment status, limited to the Buyer's company for Buyers and covering all companies with customer and status filters for staff.","id":"REQ-70","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-16","Q-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Invoice INV-000041","id":"AC-71.1","level":"api","then":"Response is application/pdf and its text contains each listed field value","when":"A Buyer of the company downloads its PDF"}],"ears":"When a Buyer of the invoiced company or a staff user downloads an invoice, the portal shall return a PDF containing the invoice number, customer, billing address, order number, invoice date, lines with quantities and prices, total and payment status.","id":"REQ-71","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","I-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Unpaid invoice INV-000041","id":"AC-72.1","level":"api","then":"Status is Paid and the invoice shows payment date 15 March recorded by S1","when":"Staff S1 marks it paid with payment date 15 March"},{"given":"Unpaid invoice INV-000041","id":"AC-72.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 403","when":"A Buyer tries to mark it paid"}],"ears":"When staff mark an invoice as paid with a payment date, the portal shall set its status to Paid and record the payment date and the user who recorded it.","id":"REQ-72","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","I-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"In March, company A: ORD-1 (2 x P @10) and ORD-2 cancelled (5 x P @10); company B: ORD-3 (1 x R @4)","id":"AC-73.1","level":"api","then":"Sales report shows A: 1 order, 20.00 and B: 1 order, 4.00; product report shows P: 2, 20.00 and R: 1, 4.00","when":"Staff run both reports for March"},{"given":"The same data","id":"AC-73.2","level":"api","then":"The CSV contains the same two rows and values","when":"Staff export the sales report as CSV"},{"given":"A signed-in Buyer","id":"AC-73.3","level":"api","then":"Response is 403","when":"The Buyer requests either report"}],"ears":"The portal shall give staff and administrators a sales report of order count and net order value per customer and a product report of quantity and net value per product, both for non-cancelled orders filtered by order date range, customer and category, each exportable as CSV with the same rows.","id":"REQ-73","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7","ASM-51"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P named 'Brake Pad'","id":"AC-74.1","level":"api","then":"An audit entry exists with A1, a timestamp, action Edit, product P and name 'Brake Pad' → 'Brake Pad Set'","when":"Administrator A1 renames it to 'Brake Pad Set'"},{"given":"Company A active","id":"AC-74.2","level":"api","then":"An audit entry records the status change by A1","when":"Administrator A1 sets it inactive"}],"ears":"When a product, category, price list or price, customer company or user is created, edited or retired, the portal shall record an audit entry with the acting user, date/time, action, record and each changed field's old and new values.","id":"REQ-74","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","Q-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Existing audit entries","id":"AC-75.1","level":"api","then":"Staff and Buyer receive 403; the Administrator receives the entries filterable by record type and date","when":"An Office Staff user and a Buyer request the audit history, then an Administrator does"}],"ears":"If a user who is not an administrator requests the audit history, then the portal shall reject the request with 403.","id":"REQ-75","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","Q-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in Administrator and category 'Filters'","id":"AC-76.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 201 and a Buyer can find it by code AF-200","when":"The Administrator creates product AF-200 with all fields"},{"given":"Existing product code AF-200","id":"AC-76.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 409","when":"Another product with code AF-200 is created"},{"given":"Product AF-200","id":"AC-76.3","level":"api","then":"It is no longer returned in Buyer search and is not deleted (admins can still view it)","when":"The Administrator retires it"}],"ears":"The portal shall let administrators add, edit and retire products with name, internal product ID, manufacturer part number, unique distributor product code, description, category, manufacturer/brand, unit of sale and pack size.","id":"REQ-76","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","I-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P with no image","id":"AC-77.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 201 and P's catalogue entry returns an image URL that serves the uploaded file","when":"The Administrator uploads a 2 MB PNG"},{"given":"Product P","id":"AC-77.2","level":"api","then":"Both are rejected with 400 and P's image is unchanged","when":"The Administrator uploads an 11 MB JPEG, then a GIF"},{"given":"Product P with image I1","id":"AC-77.3","level":"api","then":"P's catalogue entry returns I2","when":"The Administrator uploads I2"}],"ears":"When an administrator uploads a product image, the portal shall accept only JPEG, PNG or WebP files of at most 10 MB, store the image and use it as the product's displayed image in place of any earlier one.","id":"REQ-77","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","ASM-25"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in Administrator","id":"AC-78.1","level":"api","then":"Each call succeeds and the Buyer category list no longer contains 'Exhaust system'","when":"The Administrator creates 'Exhaust', renames it 'Exhaust system', then retires it"},{"given":"A signed-in Administrator","id":"AC-78.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 400","when":"The Administrator creates a category with a parent category"}],"ears":"The portal shall let administrators create, edit and retire single-level categories and assign each product to one category, excluding retired categories from Buyer category filters.","id":"REQ-78","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","I-10","ASM-48"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P","id":"AC-79.1","level":"api","then":"P's detail lists only Ford/Focus/2018 and a vehicle search for VW Golf no longer returns P","when":"The Administrator adds Ford/Focus/2018 and VW/Golf/2019, then removes VW/Golf/2019"}],"ears":"The portal shall let administrators add and remove multiple vehicle compatibility entries (make, model, year, engine, fuel type, variant) on each product.","id":"REQ-79","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","I-10","ASM-49"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Cutoff 14:00","id":"AC-80.1","level":"api","then":"The first available date is Wednesday","when":"An Administrator sets the cutoff to 12:00 and a Buyer requests available dates on Monday 13:00"},{"given":"A signed-in Office Staff user","id":"AC-80.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 403","when":"The user updates any system setting"}],"ears":"The portal shall let administrators configure the order cutoff time, business timezone, weekly non-working days, holiday dates, maximum delivery days ahead, low-stock threshold, invoice payment term days, order and invoice number prefixes, reset-link validity and invitation validity.","id":"REQ-80","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","ASM-37","ASM-38","ASM-36","Q-3","ASM-43","ASM-46"]}],"suggestions":["Let signed-in users change their own password and profile details, with the current password required.","Add a session idle timeout (for example 30 minutes) and an absolute session lifetime.","Add multi-factor authentication for Administrator and Office Staff accounts.","Add the Customer Account Manager role later on top of the role model (Q-1).","Alert admins by email when a nightly stock import fails or no file arrives.","Send email reminders for overdue invoices.","Let admins bulk-import compatibility data and products from CSV.","Agree with the client on the exact delivery-list CSV columns and ERP file format before go-live."]},{"assumptions":["Saved basket templates are in scope and shared with the whole company: Q-7 (a human answer) asks how templates are shared, which only makes sense if they are being built, so it overrides ASM-1 (out of scope).","Prices are tax-exclusive and no tax is calculated (ASM-39). This overrides ASM-6 (one configurable tax rate on invoices).","Each user keeps one saved basket across sign-ins (ASM-40). This overrides ASM-14 (basket kept for the session only).","Out-of-stock handling combines ASM-4 and ASM-33: Out of stock products can't be added and checkout is blocked for them, but quantities are not checked against imported stock.","Staff can cancel only from Received or Confirmed (Q-6). This overrides ASM-11.","When a company is inactive, its users can't sign in at all (Q-8). This overrides ASM-19.","The request says there are no online card payments in this phase, so ASM-23 (Stripe) is ignored. Marking an invoice paid records only the payment date and the user.","There are three exposed roles: Customer Buyer, Office Staff and Administrator. ASM-45 ('administrator and standard user') doesn't match the request and is ignored. Administrators are also assumed to have every Office Staff permission.","Only Administrators maintain customer company records (ASM-2). Delivery addresses are maintained by both Office Staff and Administrators (Q-5).","Order emails go to the user who placed the order. For staff-created orders they go to the company's contact email.","The vehicle compatibility entry includes an optional fuel type so vehicle search can filter on it (request §7.4).","Saturday and Sunday are the default weekly non-working days.","Repeating an order replaces the current basket contents, following the request's 'new basket' wording.","Product images may be JPEG, PNG or WebP, up to 10 MB (ASM-25).","There is one currency, with amounts in 2 decimal places.","On first deployment there is one seed Administrator account (ASM-15).","Reports are available to Office Staff and Administrators. There is no separate management role.","Retired categories are hidden from the customer filter, and their products keep their category assignment.","The stock CSV matches products on the distributor product code (ASM-7, ASM-34).","Invoice PDFs use the portal's own layout, not a reproduced client template.","The order note is optional and up to 1,000 characters."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"p95 response time ≤ 2 s","text":"Catalogue search, category filter and vehicle search respond within the target with 50,000 active products and 100 concurrent users."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"p95 response time ≤ 1 s","text":"All other read endpoints (order lists, order detail, invoices, basket) respond within the target at 100 concurrent users."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"≤ 10 minutes per run","text":"The nightly stock import of a 50,000-row file completes within the target."},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"≤ 5 minutes for 99% of emails","text":"Transactional emails (reset, invitation, amendment, confirmation, rejection, out for delivery) are handed to the email service within the target after the triggering event."},{"id":"NFR-5","metric":"0 plaintext passwords in storage; TLS 1.2 or higher on 100% of endpoints","text":"Passwords are stored only as salted hashes (bcrypt cost ≥ 12 or Argon2id) and all traffic uses HTTPS."},{"id":"NFR-6","metric":"session ends after 60 minutes without activity","text":"Idle authenticated sessions expire."},{"id":"NFR-7","metric":"≥ 99.5% monthly uptime","text":"Portal availability during the month, excluding announced maintenance."},{"id":"NFR-8","metric":"0 WCAG 2.1 AA failures in a manual audit plus automated axe scan of these flows","text":"Main flows (sign-in, catalogue, basket, checkout, orders, invoices, staff queue) meet WCAG 2.1 AA."},{"id":"NFR-9","metric":"100% of main-flow checks pass in 8 browser versions","text":"The portal works in the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari and Firefox."},{"id":"NFR-10","metric":"p95 ≤ 5 s per PDF","text":"Invoice PDF downloads are generated within the target."},{"id":"NFR-11","metric":"100% of customer endpoints covered by an automated test that another company's record returns 404","text":"Cross-company data isolation is verified for every customer-facing endpoint."}],"outOfScope":["Exposing the Customer Account Manager role in this release (Q-1)","Customers creating or editing their own delivery addresses (Q-5)","Backorders (request §8: out of scope unless separately agreed)","Online card payments and any payment provider integration (request §32; ASM-23 overridden by the request)","Tax calculation on prices, orders or invoices (ASM-39)","Volume pricing, promotional pricing, discounts and price effective dates (request §10: one price per product per price list)","Writing anything back to the ERP; the portal only reads the stock file (request §9)","Route planning for deliveries (request §22)","SMS or push notifications; email from fixed templates only (ASM-42)","Migrating existing customers, products, price lists or compatibility data; the system starts empty with seed data (ASM-15)","Nested categories (ASM-48)","Bulk import of vehicle compatibility data; entered by hand (ASM-49)","Full-text search engine and relevance ranking (ASM-50)","Custom report builder (ASM-51)","Pending or pro-forma invoices before delivery (ASM-30)","Languages other than English and multiple currencies (ASM-53)"],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active Customer Buyer buyer@acme.test with password 'Correct#Pass1' belonging to active company ACME","id":"AC-1.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 200, a session cookie is set and the body contains role 'CustomerBuyer'; GET /me with the cookie returns 200 with the buyer's email","when":"POST /auth/sign-in with those credentials"}],"ears":"When a user submits the email address and password of an active account whose customer company (if any) is active, the portal shall create an authenticated session and return the user's role.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active user buyer@acme.test exists and no user unknown@acme.test exists","id":"AC-2.1","level":"api","then":"Both responses are 401 with identical bodies containing 'invalid email or password' and no session cookie is set","when":"POST /auth/sign-in once with buyer@acme.test and a wrong password and once with unknown@acme.test"}],"ears":"If a sign-in request has an unknown email address or a wrong password, then the portal shall reject it with the same 'invalid email or password' message and status for both cases.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An active user with 4 consecutive failed sign-ins","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"The 5th attempt returns 423 with 'temporarily locked'; the correct-password attempt at 14 minutes also returns 423 and no session is created","when":"A 5th sign-in with a wrong password is made, then 14 minutes later a sign-in with the correct password is made"},{"given":"An account locked at 10:00","id":"AC-3.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 200 and a session is created; the failed-attempt counter is reset to 0","when":"A sign-in with the correct password is made at 10:16"},{"given":"A user with 4 consecutive failed sign-ins","id":"AC-3.3","level":"api","then":"The account is not locked (the counter restarted after the success)","when":"The user signs in successfully and then fails once"}],"ears":"If an account reaches 5 consecutive failed sign-in attempts, then the portal shall lock the account for 15 minutes and reject every sign-in attempt for it during that period with a 'temporarily locked' message.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-20"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"User buyer@acme.test exists and no user unknown@acme.test exists","id":"AC-4.1","level":"api","then":"Both responses are 202 with identical bodies; exactly one reset email is sent to the email service, addressed to buyer@acme.test, and none to unknown@acme.test","when":"POST /auth/password-reset is called for each address"},{"given":"An account that is currently locked by failed sign-ins","id":"AC-4.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 202 and a reset email is sent","when":"POST /auth/password-reset is called for its email"}],"ears":"When a user requests a password reset for an email address, the portal shall send a reset email containing a single-use link valid for the configured period (default 1 hour) if the address belongs to an account, and return the same response whether or not it does.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-46"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A locked account and a reset link issued 30 minutes ago","id":"AC-5.1","level":"api","then":"The reset returns 200, sign-in with the new password returns 200 and the old password returns 401","when":"The new password 'New#Pass2026' is submitted with the link and the user signs in with it"},{"given":"A reset link issued 61 minutes ago with a 1-hour expiry","id":"AC-5.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 400 'link expired' and the password is unchanged","when":"A new password is submitted with it"},{"given":"A reset link that has already been used","id":"AC-5.3","level":"api","then":"Response is 400 and the password is unchanged","when":"A new password is submitted with it again"}],"ears":"When a user submits a new password with a valid, unused and unexpired reset link, the portal shall set the new password, invalidate the link and clear any sign-in lock on the account.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-21","ASM-47","ASM-46"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Administrator session and active company ACME","id":"AC-6.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 201, a user with status 'Invited' is listed under ACME and one invitation email to new@acme.test is sent to the email service","when":"POST /admin/invitations with email new@acme.test, name, role 'CustomerBuyer' and company ACME"},{"given":"An Administrator session","id":"AC-6.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 400 and no user or email is created","when":"POST /admin/invitations with role 'CustomerAccountManager'"},{"given":"An Office Staff session","id":"AC-6.3","level":"api","then":"Response is 403","when":"POST /admin/invitations"}],"ears":"When an Administrator invites a user as Customer Buyer (with a customer company) or Office Staff, the portal shall create a pending invitation valid for the configured period (default 7 days) and send an invitation email to the invited address.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","ASM-46","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An invitation created 2 days ago","id":"AC-7.1","level":"api","then":"Both calls return 200 and the user's status is 'Active'","when":"The invitee submits password 'Start#Pass2026' with the link and then signs in"},{"given":"An invitation created 8 days ago with a 7-day expiry","id":"AC-7.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 400 'invitation expired' and the user remains 'Invited'","when":"The invitee submits a password with the link"}],"ears":"When an invited user sets a password through a valid, unexpired invitation link, the portal shall make the account active.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-46"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A pending invitation with link L1","id":"AC-8.1","level":"api","then":"A new email with link L2 is sent; using L1 returns 400; using L2 activates the account","when":"An Administrator calls POST /admin/invitations/{id}/resend and the invitee then uses L1"}],"ears":"When an Administrator resends a pending invitation, the portal shall send a new invitation link and invalidate the earlier link.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-46"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A buyer with 3 past orders whose account an Administrator deactivated","id":"AC-9.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 401 'account inactive'; Office Staff GET /staff/orders?customer=ACME still lists the 3 orders","when":"The buyer signs in with correct credentials"},{"given":"Company ACME set to inactive and an ACME buyer with an open session","id":"AC-9.2","level":"api","then":"Sign-in returns 401 and the old session returns 401","when":"The buyer signs in again, and separately calls GET /orders with the old session"},{"given":"Company ACME reactivated by an Administrator","id":"AC-9.3","level":"api","then":"Response is 200 and GET /orders returns the company's past orders","when":"The ACME buyer signs in"}],"ears":"If a deactivated user, or a user whose customer company is inactive, attempts to sign in or uses an existing session, then the portal shall reject the request while keeping all of that user's historical orders and invoices.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-17","Q-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in user","id":"AC-10.1","level":"api","then":"Sign-out returns 204 and GET /me returns 401","when":"POST /auth/sign-out then GET /me with the same cookie"}],"ears":"When a user signs out, the portal shall invalidate the session so that later requests with it are rejected with 401.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"No session","id":"AC-11.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 401","when":"GET /orders"},{"given":"A Customer Buyer session","id":"AC-11.2","level":"api","then":"Each returns 403","when":"GET /staff/orders, POST /admin/products and GET /admin/audit"},{"given":"An Office Staff session","id":"AC-11.3","level":"api","then":"Response is 403","when":"POST /admin/products"}],"ears":"The portal shall allow each operation only to the roles Customer Buyer, Office Staff or Administrator that are permitted for it, returning 401 to unauthenticated requests and 403 to signed-in users of other roles.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","Q-1","ASM-45"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Company ACME with buyers B1 and B2 (B2 placed order ORD-000010) and company BETA with order ORD-000011 and invoice INV-000005","id":"AC-12.1","level":"api","then":"GET /orders includes ORD-000010 and excludes ORD-000011; the other two calls return 404","when":"B1 calls GET /orders, GET /orders/ORD-000011 and GET /invoices/INV-000005"},{"given":"An ACME buyer","id":"AC-12.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 404","when":"GET /companies/{BETA id}/addresses"}],"ears":"The portal shall return to a Customer Buyer only orders, invoices, prices, delivery addresses and account information belonging to the buyer's own customer company, answering 404 for records of any other company.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-5","Q-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Administrator session and active buyer B1","id":"AC-13.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 200 and B1 is listed with status 'Deactivated'; B1's orders remain retrievable by staff","when":"POST /admin/users/{B1}/deactivate then GET /admin/users"},{"given":"Deactivated buyer B1","id":"AC-13.2","level":"api","then":"Both return 200","when":"POST /admin/users/{B1}/reactivate and B1 signs in"},{"given":"Buyer B1 in company ACME","id":"AC-13.3","level":"api","then":"Response is 200 and B1's GET /orders now returns BETA's orders only","when":"PATCH /admin/users/{B1} with company BETA"}],"ears":"Where a user is an Administrator, the portal shall allow listing users with their account status, deactivating and reactivating users, changing a user's role between Customer Buyer and Office Staff, and associating a Customer Buyer with a customer company.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Administrator session and active price list 'Workshop A'","id":"AC-14.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 201 and GET /staff/companies/{id} by Office Staff returns these values","when":"POST /admin/companies with name 'ACME Motors', account number 'C1001', contact details, billing address and price list 'Workshop A'"},{"given":"A company with account number 'C1001' exists","id":"AC-14.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 409","when":"An Administrator creates another company with account number 'C1001'"},{"given":"An Office Staff session","id":"AC-14.3","level":"api","then":"Response is 403","when":"PATCH /admin/companies/{id}"}],"ears":"Where a user is an Administrator, the portal shall allow creating and editing customer companies with company name, unique account number, primary contact, contact email, contact phone, billing address, assigned price list and active status, while Office Staff have read-only access to them.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","I-6","ASM-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Office Staff session and company ACME","id":"AC-15.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 201 and an ACME buyer's GET /addresses lists 'Main workshop'","when":"POST /staff/companies/{ACME}/addresses with label 'Main workshop' and full address fields"},{"given":"An ACME buyer session","id":"AC-15.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 403","when":"POST /addresses or PATCH /addresses/{id}"},{"given":"An ACME address that staff retired","id":"AC-15.3","level":"api","then":"The retired address is not listed","when":"The buyer calls GET /addresses"}],"ears":"The portal shall allow only Office Staff and Administrators to create, edit and retire a customer company's delivery addresses (label, address lines 1–2, city, state/region, postal code, country, contact person, contact phone), and shall give Customer Buyers read-only access to their company's active addresses.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","I-6","Q-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Companies 'ACME Motors' (C1001) and 'Beta Fleet' (C2002)","id":"AC-16.1","level":"api","then":"The first returns only ACME Motors; the second returns only Beta Fleet","when":"Office Staff call GET /staff/companies?q=acme and GET /staff/companies?q=200"}],"ears":"When Office Staff search customers with a term, the portal shall return companies whose name or account number contains the term, ignoring case.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Administrator session and category 'Brake system'","id":"AC-17.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 201 with an internal product ID and the product appears in GET /catalogue for a buyer whose price list has a price for it","when":"POST /admin/products with name 'Front brake pad set', code 'BP-1001', MPN 'TRW-GDB1550', brand 'TRW', unit 'set', pack size 1, category 'Brake system'"},{"given":"A product with code 'BP-1001' exists","id":"AC-17.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 409","when":"An Administrator creates another product with code 'BP-1001'"}],"ears":"Where a user is an Administrator, the portal shall allow creating and editing products with name, manufacturer part number, unique distributor product code, description, category, manufacturer/brand, unit of sale, pack size and active/retired status.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product BP-1001 on delivered order ORD-000020 and invoice INV-000008, then retired by an Administrator","id":"AC-18.1","level":"api","then":"Search returns no BP-1001; add returns 400; the order and invoice still show the BP-1001 line with original price","when":"A buyer searches 'BP-1001', adds BP-1001 to the basket, and opens ORD-000020 and INV-000008"}],"ears":"While a product is retired, the portal shall exclude it from catalogue listings, search results and basket additions while still showing it on existing orders and invoices.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Administrator session","id":"AC-19.1","level":"api","then":"Create returns 201, retire returns 200, and 'Filters' is not in the buyer's category list","when":"POST /admin/categories with name 'Filters', then retire it, then a buyer calls GET /categories"}],"ears":"Where a user is an Administrator, the portal shall allow creating, editing and retiring single-level categories and assigning each product to one category, and shall exclude retired categories from the customer category list.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","I-17","ASM-48"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active products 'Front brake pad set' (code BP-1001, MPN TRW-GDB1550, brand TRW) and 'Oil filter' (code OF-200, brand Bosch)","id":"AC-20.1","level":"api","then":"'brake', 'bp-10' and 'gdb15' each return only the brake pad set; 'bosch' returns only the oil filter","when":"A buyer calls GET /catalogue?q= with 'brake', 'bp-10', 'gdb15', 'bosch'"}],"ears":"When a customer searches the catalogue with a term, the portal shall return active products whose name, distributor product code, manufacturer part number or manufacturer/brand contains the term as a case-insensitive partial match.","id":"REQ-20","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10","ASM-50"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active products in 'Brake system' (2) and 'Filters' (3)","id":"AC-21.1","level":"api","then":"The first returns the 3 filter products, the second only matching filter products, the third all 5","when":"A buyer calls GET /catalogue?category=Filters, then GET /catalogue?category=Filters&q=oil, then GET /catalogue"}],"ears":"When a customer selects a category filter, the portal shall return only active products in that category, combined with any search term, and shall return all active products again when the filter is cleared.","id":"REQ-21","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P1 compatible with Ford Focus 2018 1.0 EcoBoost petrol Titanium and product P2 compatible with Ford Focus 2015 1.6 TDCi diesel","id":"AC-22.1","level":"api","then":"The first returns P1 and P2; the second returns only P1","when":"A buyer calls GET /catalogue/vehicle?make=Ford&model=Focus, then with year=2018"},{"given":"The same compatibility data","id":"AC-22.2","level":"api","then":"The response lists 'Focus'","when":"A buyer calls GET /vehicles/models?make=Ford"}],"ears":"When a customer searches by vehicle with a make, model and optionally year, engine, fuel type and variant, the portal shall return active products having a compatibility entry that matches every selected attribute.","id":"REQ-22","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Administrator session and product P1","id":"AC-23.1","level":"api","then":"GET /catalogue/products/{P1} lists exactly the remaining entry","when":"Two compatibility entries are added to P1 and one is then removed"}],"ears":"Where a user is an Administrator, the portal shall allow adding and removing vehicle compatibility entries (make, model, model year, engine, fuel type, variant) on a product, with any number of entries per product.","id":"REQ-23","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","I-17","ASM-49"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product P1 with an existing image","id":"AC-24.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 200 and the catalogue entry for P1 returns an image URL serving the new file","when":"An Administrator uploads a 2 MB PNG"},{"given":"Product P1","id":"AC-24.2","level":"api","then":"Both return 400 and P1's image is unchanged","when":"An Administrator uploads an 11 MB JPEG, and separately a .exe file"}],"ears":"When an Administrator uploads a product image, the portal shall accept JPEG, PNG or WebP files up to 10 MB, store the file, and replace any previous image of that product.","id":"REQ-24","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","I-10","ASM-25"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active product P1 priced at 42.50 on the buyer's price list with stock status 'Low stock'","id":"AC-25.1","level":"api","then":"The list entry contains imageUrl, name, code, manufacturer, unit, packSize, price 42.50 and stockStatus 'Low stock'; the detail additionally contains description and compatibility entries","when":"The buyer calls GET /catalogue and GET /catalogue/products/{P1}"}],"ears":"When a customer lists the catalogue or opens a product, the portal shall return image URL, name, product code, manufacturer, unit, pack size, the customer's price and stock status for each product, plus description and vehicle compatibility on the product detail.","id":"REQ-25","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-10","I-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Administrator session","id":"AC-26.1","level":"api","then":"The list contains a single P1 price of 37.00","when":"Create price list 'Fleet', set P1 at 39.00, edit it to 38.00, then set P1 again at 37.00"},{"given":"Price list 'Fleet'","id":"AC-26.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 400","when":"An Administrator sets a price of -1.00 or 0"}],"ears":"Where a user is an Administrator, the portal shall allow creating and renaming price lists, setting, editing and removing one price per product per price list, and assigning a price list to a customer company.","id":"REQ-26","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-17"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"P1 priced 42.50 on 'Standard' (assigned to ACME) and 38.00 on 'Fleet' (assigned to BETA)","id":"AC-27.1","level":"api","then":"ACME sees 42.50 and BETA sees 38.00; neither response contains the other price","when":"An ACME buyer and a BETA buyer each call GET /catalogue/products/{P1}"},{"given":"An Administrator changes ACME's price list to 'Fleet'","id":"AC-27.2","level":"api","then":"The price shown is 38.00","when":"The ACME buyer calls GET /catalogue/products/{P1}"}],"ears":"When a Customer Buyer views a product, the portal shall show the price from the price list assigned to the buyer's company.","id":"REQ-27","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-11"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Active product P2 not on ACME's price list","id":"AC-28.1","level":"api","then":"P2 is listed with price null and priceLabel 'price on request'; the add returns 400","when":"An ACME buyer lists the catalogue and calls POST /basket/lines for P2"}],"ears":"If an active product has no price on the customer's assigned price list, then the portal shall show it as 'price on request' and reject adding it to the basket.","id":"REQ-28","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-11","ASM-31","ASM-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Price list 'Fleet' assigned to active company BETA, and price list 'Old' assigned to no active company","id":"AC-29.1","level":"api","then":"'Fleet' returns 409 naming BETA and stays active; 'Old' returns 200 and becomes inactive","when":"An Administrator deactivates 'Fleet' and then 'Old'"}],"ears":"If an Administrator deactivates a price list that is assigned to any active customer company, then the portal shall reject the deactivation.","id":"REQ-29","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-17","ASM-44"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Products BP-1001 (qty 10) and OF-200 (qty 0), low-stock threshold 5, and a file with rows BP-1001,3 and OF-200,50","id":"AC-30.1","level":"job","then":"BP-1001 has quantity 3 and status 'Low stock', OF-200 has 50 and 'In stock', and an import record with status 'Succeeded' and 2 rows imported exists","when":"The stock import job runs"}],"ears":"When the scheduled stock import job runs and finds a valid ERP CSV file (product code, quantity) in the configured folder or SFTP location, the portal shall replace the stock quantity of every matching product with the file value and recalculate its stock status.","id":"REQ-30","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","I-3","ASM-34","ASM-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Threshold 5","id":"AC-31.1","level":"unit","then":"Results are Out of stock, Low stock, Low stock, In stock","when":"StockStatusPolicy.statusFor(quantity, 5) is called with 0, 1, 5 and 6"}],"ears":"The portal shall derive stock status as Out of stock for quantity 0 or less, Low stock for quantity from 1 up to and including the configured low-stock threshold, and In stock above the threshold.","id":"REQ-31","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-12","ASM-36","ASM-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Products BP-1001 (qty 10) and OF-200 (qty 7), and a file with rows BP-1001,4 and ZZ-999,8","id":"AC-32.1","level":"job","then":"BP-1001 is 4, OF-200 stays 7, and the import record shows 1 row imported and 1 row skipped listing 'ZZ-999'","when":"The stock import job runs"}],"ears":"While importing a valid stock file, the portal shall skip and log rows whose product code is unknown and leave the stock of products absent from the file unchanged.","id":"REQ-32","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","ASM-35","ASM-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"BP-1001 has qty 10 and the file contains BP-1001,4 and OF-200,abc","id":"AC-33.1","level":"job","then":"BP-1001 stays 10 and an import record with status 'Failed' and a reason naming the invalid quantity row exists","when":"The stock import job runs"},{"given":"No file in the configured location","id":"AC-33.2","level":"job","then":"No stock changes and an import record with status 'Failed' and reason 'file not found' exists","when":"The stock import job runs"}],"ears":"If the stock file is missing, empty, lacks the product code or quantity column, or has any non-integer quantity, then the portal shall keep all previous stock data unchanged and record the import as failed with the reason.","id":"REQ-33","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"One succeeded import yesterday and one failed import today","id":"AC-34.1","level":"api","then":"Two records are returned, today's failed one first with its reason","when":"Office Staff call GET /staff/stock-imports"}],"ears":"When Office Staff or an Administrator request the stock import history, the portal shall return each import's start time, status, rows imported, rows skipped and failure reason, newest first.","id":"REQ-34","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12","I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A buyer with an empty basket and P1 priced 42.50","id":"AC-35.1","level":"api","then":"The basket shows P1 qty 3, unit price 42.50, line total 127.50, subtotal 127.50","when":"POST /basket/lines P1 qty 2, PATCH qty to 3, sign out, sign in, GET /basket"},{"given":"A basket with P1","id":"AC-35.2","level":"api","then":"The PATCH calls return 400; DELETE returns 204 and the subtotal is 0.00","when":"PATCH the P1 quantity to 0 or 1.5, and separately DELETE the P1 line"}],"ears":"The portal shall keep one basket per Customer Buyer across sign-ins, supporting adding a product with a positive whole quantity, changing a quantity, removing a line, and returning each line's unit price and line total and the basket subtotal.","id":"REQ-35","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-40"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Product OF-200 with status Out of stock","id":"AC-36.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 400 with 'out of stock' and the basket is unchanged; GET /catalogue still lists OF-200 as 'Out of stock'","when":"A buyer calls POST /basket/lines for OF-200"}],"ears":"If a customer tries to add a product whose stock status is Out of stock to the basket, then the portal shall reject the addition with an 'out of stock' message.","id":"REQ-36","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-13","ASM-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A basket with P1 (In stock) and BP-1001 which became Out of stock after it was added","id":"AC-37.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 409 listing BP-1001 and no order is created; after removing BP-1001 the submission succeeds","when":"The buyer submits the order"},{"given":"P1 with imported quantity 3 and status Low stock","id":"AC-37.2","level":"api","then":"The order is created","when":"The buyer submits an order for P1 qty 10"}],"ears":"If the basket contains a product that is Out of stock, retired or without a price at checkout, then the portal shall block order submission and identify those lines, without checking quantities against imported stock.","id":"REQ-37","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","I-3","ASM-33","ASM-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"P1 added at 42.50, then an Administrator changes it to 45.00","id":"AC-38.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 409 with P1 old 42.50 and new 45.00 and no order is created; GET /basket shows 45.00; resubmitting with the confirmation flag creates the order at 45.00","when":"The buyer submits the order"}],"ears":"If a basket price differs from the current price on the customer's price list at checkout, then the portal shall update the basket to the current price, return the old and new prices, and reject submission until the customer confirms again.","id":"REQ-38","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","I-11","ASM-32"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A basket with P1 qty 2, address 'Main workshop', date 2026-10-07 and note 'Rear door'","id":"AC-39.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 200 containing these values and subtotal 85.00, and GET /orders shows no new order","when":"POST /checkout/review"}],"ears":"When a customer requests a checkout review, the portal shall return the basket lines, prices, subtotal, selected delivery address, selected delivery date and note without creating an order.","id":"REQ-39","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","I-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Cutoff 14:00, business timezone configured, Saturday and Sunday non-working, no holidays","id":"AC-40.1","level":"unit","then":"Results are Tue 10-06, Wed 10-07, Wed 10-07, Mon 10-12 and Tue 10-13","when":"DeliveryDateCalculator.earliestDeliveryDate is called for Mon 2026-10-05 13:00, Mon 14:00, Mon 15:00, Fri 2026-10-09 13:00 and Fri 15:00 (business time)"},{"given":"Tue 2026-10-06 configured as a holiday","id":"AC-40.2","level":"unit","then":"Result is Wed 2026-10-07","when":"earliestDeliveryDate is called for Mon 2026-10-05 13:00"},{"given":"Cutoff 14:00 and a server clock in UTC while the business timezone is UTC+3","id":"AC-40.3","level":"unit","then":"Result is Tue 2026-10-06","when":"earliestDeliveryDate is called for 2026-10-05 10:30 UTC (13:30 business time)"}],"ears":"The portal shall calculate the earliest delivery date as the next working day for orders placed before the configured cutoff (default 14:00) and the working day after the next working day for orders placed at or after it, using the configured business timezone, weekly non-working days and holiday dates.","id":"REQ-40","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-37","ASM-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Order placed Mon 2026-10-05 15:00 with Saturday/Sunday non-working and maximum 30 days","id":"AC-41.1","level":"api","then":"The first three return 400 and create no order; Wed 10-07 creates the order","when":"Submission with delivery date Tue 10-06, Sat 10-10, Thu 11-05, and Wed 10-07"}],"ears":"If a submitted delivery date is not a working day, is earlier than the earliest delivery date, or is more than the configured maximum days ahead (default 30), then the portal shall reject the order submission.","id":"REQ-41","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","ASM-38"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An ACME buyer and a BETA address id","id":"AC-42.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 400 and no order is created","when":"The buyer submits an order with the BETA address"}],"ears":"If a submitted delivery address is not an active address of the customer's company, then the portal shall reject the order submission.","id":"REQ-42","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","Q-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Last order number ORD-000122, prefix 'ORD-', basket P1 qty 2 at 42.50, a valid address and date","id":"AC-43.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 201 with number ORD-000123, status Received, line P1 qty 2 unit 42.50 total 85.00, the note stored; GET /basket is empty; GET /staff/orders lists ORD-000123","when":"The buyer submits the order with note 'Rear door'"}],"ears":"When a customer submits a valid order, the portal shall create it with the next sequential order number using the configured prefix, store lines with order-time prices, delivery address, delivery date and optional note, set status Received, empty the basket and include it in the Office Staff order queue.","id":"REQ-43","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-4","I-13","ASM-43","ASM-24"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"ORD-000123 with P1 at 42.50","id":"AC-44.1","level":"api","then":"GET /orders/ORD-000123 still shows P1 at 42.50 and total 85.00","when":"An Administrator changes P1 to 50.00 and reassigns ACME to another price list"}],"ears":"While an order exists, the portal shall keep its stored order-time line prices unchanged when price lists are later edited or reassigned.","id":"REQ-44","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"ACME buyers B1 and B2 and BETA buyer B3; B1's basket has P1 qty 4","id":"AC-45.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 201; B2's GET /templates lists it with P1 qty 4; B3's GET /templates does not","when":"B1 calls POST /templates with name 'Weekly Workshop Order'"},{"given":"An ACME template","id":"AC-45.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 204 and it no longer appears for B1","when":"B2 deletes it"}],"ears":"When a Customer Buyer saves the basket as a named template, the portal shall store the template's products and quantities and make it visible to all users of the same customer company.","id":"REQ-45","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","Q-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Template with P1 qty 4 (now priced 45.00) and BP-1001 qty 2 (now retired)","id":"AC-46.1","level":"api","then":"The basket contains P1 qty 4 at 45.00 and the response lists BP-1001 as 'no longer available'","when":"The buyer calls POST /templates/{id}/add-to-basket"}],"ears":"When a customer adds a template to the basket, the portal shall add its active, priced, not-out-of-stock products at current prices and return the products that were not added with the reason.","id":"REQ-46","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-13","Q-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The order status rules","id":"AC-47.1","level":"unit","then":"Results are true, true, false, false, true, false, false","when":"OrderStatusMachine.canTransition is called for Received→Confirmed, Confirmed→Picking, Received→Picking, Picking→Confirmed, Confirmed→Cancelled, Picking→Cancelled, Delivered→Cancelled"},{"given":"Order ORD-000123 in Picking","id":"AC-47.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 409 and the status stays Picking","when":"Office Staff call POST /staff/orders/ORD-000123/status with 'Delivered'"}],"ears":"The portal shall allow order status changes only one step forward along Received, Confirmed, Picking, Out for delivery, Delivered, plus a change to Cancelled only from Received or Confirmed.","id":"REQ-47","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","Q-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"ORD-000123 placed by buyer B1 and confirmed by staff S1","id":"AC-48.1","level":"api","then":"The timeline lists Received by B1 and Confirmed by S1 with timestamps in order","when":"B1 calls GET /orders/ORD-000123"}],"ears":"When an order changes status, the portal shall append a timeline entry with the new status, date/time and the user or 'system' that made the change, visible on the order detail.","id":"REQ-48","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","I-8","I-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Received order ORD-000123 with P1 qty 2","id":"AC-49.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 200, the total is 42.50 and the order detail shows amendment 'P1 quantity 2→1 by S1' with time","when":"Staff S1 calls PATCH /staff/orders/ORD-000123 setting P1 qty to 1"},{"given":"Order ORD-000124 in Confirmed","id":"AC-49.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 409 and the order is unchanged","when":"Staff attempt to change a quantity"}],"ears":"While an order is Received, the portal shall allow Office Staff to change line quantities, remove lines, change the delivery date (subject to the delivery date rules), change the delivery address (to an active address of the company) and edit the note, recording each change with field, old value, new value, user and time.","id":"REQ-49","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","I-4","I-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Received order ORD-000123 placed by B1 with P1 qty 2","id":"AC-50.1","level":"api","then":"One email to B1's address is sent to the email service containing 'ORD-000123' and 'P1' with 2 and 1","when":"Staff change P1 to qty 1"}],"ears":"When Office Staff save a quantity change or line removal on an order, the portal shall send the customer an email listing each changed product with old and new quantity.","id":"REQ-50","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","ASM-42"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Received order ORD-000123 with an amended quantity","id":"AC-51.1","level":"api","then":"Status is Confirmed with S1 and time recorded, and one email containing ORD-000123, lines, date, address, total and the amendment is sent","when":"Staff S1 calls POST /staff/orders/ORD-000123/confirm"},{"given":"Received order containing a product now Out of stock","id":"AC-51.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 409 naming the product and the status stays Received with no email","when":"Staff confirm it"}],"ears":"When Office Staff confirm a Received order that has no Out of stock or retired products and whose company is active, the portal shall set it to Confirmed, record the confirming user and time, and send the customer a confirmation email with the order number, lines, delivery date, delivery address, total and any staff amendments.","id":"REQ-51","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","I-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Received order ORD-000123","id":"AC-52.1","level":"api","then":"Status is Cancelled, the timeline marks it staff-rejected with the reason and user, and one email containing 'Account on hold' is sent","when":"Staff call POST /staff/orders/ORD-000123/reject with reason 'Account on hold'"},{"given":"Received order","id":"AC-52.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 400 and the status is unchanged","when":"Staff call reject without a reason"}],"ears":"When Office Staff reject or cancel an order in Received or Confirmed status with a reason, the portal shall set it to Cancelled marked as staff-rejected with the reason, user and time, and email the customer the reason.","id":"REQ-52","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-14","ASM-41","ASM-12","Q-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Order ORD-000123 in Picking","id":"AC-53.1","level":"api","then":"One email containing 'ORD-000123' and 'out for delivery' is sent to the customer","when":"Staff change the status to Out for delivery"}],"ears":"When an order changes to Out for delivery, the portal shall send the customer an email identifying the order number and stating that it is out for delivery.","id":"REQ-53","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-14","ASM-42"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Orders for ACME (Received, 2026-10-05) and BETA (Confirmed, 2026-10-06)","id":"AC-54.1","level":"api","then":"Each returns only the matching single order with all six fields","when":"GET /staff/orders?customer=ACME, ?status=Confirmed and ?from=2026-10-06&to=2026-10-06"}],"ears":"When Office Staff open the order queue, the portal shall list all orders with order number, customer, order date, requested delivery date, order total and current status, filterable by customer, order date range and status.","id":"REQ-54","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Staff S1 at Mon 15:00 and company ACME with P1 at 42.50","id":"AC-55.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 201 with status Received, price 42.50, createdBy S1; an ACME buyer's GET /orders lists it","when":"POST /staff/orders for ACME with P1 qty 2, an ACME address and date Wed"},{"given":"Staff at Mon 15:00","id":"AC-55.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 400","when":"POST /staff/orders with delivery date Tue"}],"ears":"When Office Staff submit an order on behalf of a customer company, the portal shall apply that company's prices, the delivery date, address and stock rules used for customer orders, record that it was created by the staff user, and show it in the company's order history.","id":"REQ-55","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","I-14","ASM-10"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"ACME orders by B1 (Received) and B2 (Delivered)","id":"AC-56.1","level":"api","then":"The first returns both orders with all six fields; the second only B2's","when":"B1 calls GET /orders and GET /orders?status=Delivered"}],"ears":"When a Customer Buyer lists orders, the portal shall return all of the company's orders with order number, order date, delivery date, delivery address, total and status, filterable by order date range and status.","id":"REQ-56","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-15","Q-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Amended order ORD-000123","id":"AC-57.1","level":"api","then":"All listed fields are present, including the amendment entries","when":"An ACME buyer calls GET /orders/ORD-000123"}],"ears":"When a user permitted to see an order opens it, the portal shall return the order number, order date, customer, delivery address, requested delivery date, current status, status timeline, products, quantities, unit prices, line totals, order total, note and staff amendments.","id":"REQ-57","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"ACME order ORD-000123 in Received","id":"AC-58.1","level":"api","then":"Status is Cancelled and the timeline records the buyer","when":"An ACME buyer calls POST /orders/ORD-000123/cancel"},{"given":"ACME order ORD-000124 in Confirmed","id":"AC-58.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 409 with 'contact the distributor office' and the status stays Confirmed","when":"The buyer calls cancel"}],"ears":"When a Customer Buyer cancels an order of their company, the portal shall cancel it only if it is in Received status and otherwise reject the cancellation with a message to contact the distributor office.","id":"REQ-58","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Delivered order with P1 qty 2 at 42.50 (now 45.00) and BP-1001 qty 1 (now retired)","id":"AC-59.1","level":"api","then":"The basket has only P1 qty 2 at 45.00, the response flags BP-1001 as unavailable, and the order count is unchanged","when":"The buyer calls POST /orders/{id}/repeat"}],"ears":"When a Customer Buyer repeats a previous order, the portal shall replace the basket contents with that order's active, priced, not-out-of-stock products at current prices and original quantities, return the products that could not be added, and create no order.","id":"REQ-59","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Order ORD-000123 Out for delivery, total 85.00, last invoice INV-000122","id":"AC-60.1","level":"api","then":"Invoice INV-000123 exists for ORD-000123 with the company billing address, the order lines, total 85.00, no tax line and status Unpaid","when":"Staff change the status to Delivered"},{"given":"Order ORD-000123 in Picking","id":"AC-60.2","level":"api","then":"No invoice for ORD-000123 is listed","when":"The buyer lists invoices"}],"ears":"When an order becomes Delivered, the portal shall create exactly one invoice for it with the next sequential invoice number using the configured prefix, customer, billing address, order number, invoice date, lines with quantities and prices, tax-exclusive total and status Unpaid.","id":"REQ-60","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","ASM-43","ASM-39","ASM-22"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Unpaid invoice dated 2026-03-01 and term 30 days","id":"AC-61.1","level":"unit","then":"Results are Unpaid and Overdue","when":"InvoiceStatusPolicy.statusFor is called for 2026-03-31 and 2026-04-01"},{"given":"An invoice dated 2026-03-01 marked paid on 2026-04-10","id":"AC-61.2","level":"unit","then":"Result is Paid","when":"statusFor is called for 2026-04-15"}],"ears":"While an invoice is unpaid and the current business date is later than its invoice date plus the configured payment term (default 30 days), the portal shall report its status as Overdue.","id":"REQ-61","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Unpaid invoice INV-000123","id":"AC-62.1","level":"api","then":"Status is Paid with payment date 2026-10-04 and recordedBy S1","when":"Staff S1 call POST /staff/invoices/INV-000123/mark-paid with date 2026-10-04 on 2026-10-04"},{"given":"A paid invoice, and separately an unpaid one","id":"AC-62.2","level":"api","then":"Both return 400 and nothing changes","when":"Staff mark the paid one paid again, and the unpaid one with a future date"}],"ears":"When Office Staff mark an unpaid or overdue invoice as paid with a payment date not later than today, the portal shall set it to Paid and store the payment date and the recording user.","id":"REQ-62","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","I-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"ACME invoices INV-000120 (Paid) and INV-000123 (Unpaid), and a BETA invoice","id":"AC-63.1","level":"api","then":"Exactly the two ACME invoices are returned with their statuses","when":"An ACME buyer calls GET /invoices"}],"ears":"When a Customer Buyer lists invoices, the portal shall return every existing invoice of the company with invoice number, invoice date, order number, total and payment status.","id":"REQ-63","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-16","ASM-30","Q-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Invoice INV-000123","id":"AC-64.1","level":"api","then":"Response is 200 with content type application/pdf and the extracted text contains all listed fields","when":"An ACME buyer calls GET /invoices/INV-000123/pdf"}],"ears":"When a Customer Buyer of the invoice's company or Office Staff downloads an invoice PDF, the portal shall return a PDF containing the invoice number, customer, billing address, order number, invoice date, lines with quantities and prices, total and payment status.","id":"REQ-64","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-16","I-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Orders for 2026-10-07 in Confirmed, Picking, Received and Delivered","id":"AC-65.1","level":"api","then":"The CSV has a header with the listed columns and rows only for the Confirmed and Picking orders","when":"GET /staff/delivery-list.csv?date=2026-10-07"}],"ears":"When Office Staff export the delivery list for a date (default today), the portal shall return a CSV of orders with that delivery date in Confirmed, Picking or Out for delivery status, with order number, customer, delivery address, contact person, contact phone, delivery date, order lines, note and status.","id":"REQ-65","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","ASM-52"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"2 Received, 1 Picking, 1 Out for delivery, 1 order due today, 3 unpaid invoices and a failed last import","id":"AC-66.1","level":"api","then":"The response shows 2, 1, 1, 1, 3 and lastImport status 'Failed' with its time","when":"GET /staff/dashboard"}],"ears":"When Office Staff open the dashboard, the portal shall return counts of Received, Picking and Out for delivery orders, orders due for delivery today, unpaid or overdue invoices, and the status and time of the most recent stock import.","id":"REQ-66","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"In October ACME has orders of 85.00 and 15.00 and one cancelled order of 50.00; P1 sold qty 2 for 85.00","id":"AC-67.1","level":"api","then":"Sales shows ACME 2 orders 100.00; products shows P1 qty 2 value 85.00","when":"GET /reports/sales?from=2026-10-01&to=2026-10-31 and GET /reports/products with the same range"},{"given":"The same data","id":"AC-67.2","level":"api","then":"The CSV contains the same rows and values","when":"GET /reports/sales.csv for the same range"}],"ears":"When Office Staff or an Administrator request the sales or product report for a date range, the portal shall return, excluding Cancelled orders, order count and total value per customer (sales) and quantity and value per product (product), filterable by customer and category and exportable as CSV with the same rows.","id":"REQ-67","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7","ASM-51","ASM-18"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Administrator A1 changes P1's price on 'Standard' from 42.50 to 45.00","id":"AC-68.1","level":"api","then":"An entry shows A1, the time, P1 price 42.50→45.00","when":"A1 calls GET /admin/audit?entity=priceList"},{"given":"An audit entry","id":"AC-68.2","level":"api","then":"The GET returns 403 and the DELETE returns 405 with the entry still present","when":"Office Staff call GET /admin/audit, and an Administrator calls DELETE /admin/audit/{id}"}],"ears":"When a product, category, price list or price, customer company or user is created, edited or retired, the portal shall record an audit entry with who, when, the entity and each changed field's old and new value, viewable only by Administrators and not editable or deletable.","id":"REQ-68","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","Q-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Administrator session and cutoff 14:00","id":"AC-69.1","level":"api","then":"The earliest offered date is Wednesday","when":"PUT /admin/settings sets cutoff 12:00 and a buyer at 13:00 Monday requests delivery options"},{"given":"An Office Staff session","id":"AC-69.2","level":"api","then":"Response is 403","when":"PUT /admin/settings"}],"ears":"Where a user is an Administrator, the portal shall allow configuring the order cutoff time, business timezone, weekly non-working days, holiday dates, maximum delivery days ahead, low-stock threshold, invoice payment term, order and invoice number prefixes, reset-link and invitation expiry, and stock file location.","id":"REQ-69","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-17","ASM-37","ASM-36","ASM-38","Q-3","ASM-43","ASM-46"]}],"suggestions":["Confirm with the client whether Administrators should have all Office Staff capabilities, since ASM-45 was answered with an unrelated default.","Confirm the tax treatment, since ASM-6 and ASM-39 contradict each other.","Consider sending an 'order received' email when an order is submitted. The request only asks for emails at confirmation, amendment, rejection and out for delivery.","Consider emailing the customer when staff change the delivery date or address, not only quantities.","Plan the Customer Account Manager role for a later release (Q-1), with permissions kept separate from Customer Buyer.","Consider a bulk CSV import for vehicle compatibility data once the catalogue grows.","Consider letting customers request address changes through the portal instead of by phone or email.","Check the dashboard widgets and delivery-list CSV columns with Office Staff before building them."]}],"models":["claude-opus-5-5","claude-opus-5-5","claude-opus-5-5"],"notes":["No OpenAI key: specify-other ran on claude-opus-5-5 (same family as the implementer)"]}